{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_0184HQkqsyZr6W4494zL1EbN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0133BHj9mHyVJnBjnQ6XZuZo","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7953,"cache_read_input_tokens":12117,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7953},"output_tokens":24,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f245fed0-0457-4d6a-9da2-744553774a6f","uuid":"9ebb4067-8591-4b01-b8d7-89447a0e9b5a"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0133BHj9mHyVJnBjnQ6XZuZo","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# 2026-04-15-1600-fix-batch-round0-revert-and-reapply\n2\t\n3\tRevert the broken batch-round0-descriptors commit (0d1bb2f9) which causes APC 300 STARK proving to hang for 12+ minutes, then re-apply the batch Round 0 path with the CPU bottleneck fixed. The existing batch code redundantly reconstructs logup interaction DAGs and rules per batchable AIR via `build_logup_rules_for_air()` (involving `SymbolicDagBuilder`, `SymbolicRulesGpu::new`, and per-AIR device uploads), which takes prohibitively long for the ~300 small AIRs at APC 300. The fix reuses the precomputed `logup_round0_buffer_size` from `AirDataGpu` and the existing per-AIR logup rule data (DAG, rules, weights) that the non-batched path already constructs during Phase 1 work-item preparation, avoiding all redundant CPU-side symbolic computation.\n4\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f245fed0-0457-4d6a-9da2-744553774a6f","uuid":"93b052b5-cff2-472c-9e6b-cd4af0d198d7","timestamp":"2026-04-15T15:27:35.265Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md","content":"# 2026-04-15-1600-fix-batch-round0-revert-and-reapply\n\nRevert the broken batch-round0-descriptors commit (0d1bb2f9) which causes APC 300 STARK proving to hang for 12+ minutes, then re-apply the batch Round 0 path with the CPU bottleneck fixed. The existing batch code redundantly reconstructs logup interaction DAGs and rules per batchable AIR via `build_logup_rules_for_air()` (involving `SymbolicDagBuilder`, `SymbolicRulesGpu::new`, and per-AIR device uploads), which takes prohibitively long for the ~300 small AIRs at APC 300. The fix reuses the precomputed `logup_round0_buffer_size` from `AirDataGpu` and the existing per-AIR logup rule data (DAG, rules, weights) that the non-batched path already constructs during Phase 1 work-item preparation, avoiding all redundant CPU-side symbolic computation.\n","numLines":4,"startLine":1,"totalLines":4}}}
