{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01JsGisQH822LNDPXcn4tRmN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have the current measurements. Let me compile a summary:\n\n**Baseline (APC 300)**:\n- STARK excl trace: 2455ms\n- Constraints: 1634ms\n- LogUp GKR: 790ms\n- Round 0: 662ms\n- MLE Rounds: 180ms\n- Openings: 413ms\n- Trace Commit: 406ms\n\n**Current (APC 300)**:\n- STARK excl trace: 1106ms (2.22x lower vs baseline)\n- Constraints: 706ms (2.31x)\n\n\n- LogUp GKR: 361ms (2.19x)\n- Round 0: 179ms (3.70x)\n- MLE Rounds: 164ms (1.10x)\n- Openings: 200ms (2.07x)\n- Trace Commit: 197ms (2.06x)\n\nFor APC 0, the baseline STARK time was 2153ms and it's now down to 1784ms, a 1.21x improvement. Looking at APC 100, the baseline sits at 2155ms.\n\nNow checking APC 100 with the current implementation—I'm seeing 1310ms, which is a 1.64x reduction from baseline. The real question is whether STARK is scaling properly with the cell and message reductions we're getting from APC 0 to APC 300. The cells dropped 2.34x, bus messages fell 2.15x, and constraint instances decreased 2.24x, but the baseline STARK time barely improved or even got slightly worse going from APC 0 to APC 300. With the current implementation though, I'm getting 1.61x improvement across that range, which is progress but still not matching the theoretical scaling we should see from those reductions.\n\nAt APC 300, the 1106ms breaks down with constraints dominating at 706ms—LogUp GKR alone is taking 361ms, which is the biggest single bottleneck I need to address.\n\nLooking at how these components scale from APC 0 to APC 300, I see some concerning patterns: LogUp GKR only achieves 1.95x speedup when I need better scaling, Trace Commit is doing well at 2.42x, but Round 0 isn't scaling at all—it's basically flat at 178-179ms. MLE Rounds also seems to be underperforming on the scaling front. The MLE rounds are actually performing worse with APC 300 due to the increased number of AIR instances creating more per-instance overhead, and Stacked Reduction isn't scaling either. The biggest bottleneck is LogUp GKR at 361ms, so I need to figure out which components should be scaling but aren't. Let me run nsight profiling on APC 300 to see what's happening at the GPU level, though I should first verify if my previous nsight data is still relevant or if I need fresh profiling data.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":889,"cache_read_input_tokens":66907,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":889},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f245fed0-0457-4d6a-9da2-744553774a6f","uuid":"27c58fe4-52e7-477c-a282-9ad3c1f7d691"}
