eight initially\n     * num_x = interpolated evaluation points = sp_deg (constraint_degree)\n     * These are interpolated values NOT the full folded evaluations\n\n4. INTERPOLATION KERNEL\n   Location: /home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs:1766-1772\n   - batched_interpolate_columns_matrix_kernel\n   - Interpolates matrices to sp_deg * num_y points (line 1786)\n   - Line 1786: interpolated_height = sp_deg * meta.num_y\n   - This runs ONCE per round before batch MLE evaluation\n\n5. HOW WORK SCALES WITH MORE AIRs\n   \n   a) NUM_X: CONSTANT (sp_deg = constraint_degree, does NOT depend on AIR count)\n      - Only depends on constraint degree (fixed per protocol)\n   \n   b) NUM_Y: PER-AIR, VARIES BY TRACE HEIGHT\n      - Each AIR has its own num_y based on its height and round number\n      - Smaller-height AIRs finish earlier (when round > n_lift)\n   \n   c) BLOCK COUNT: SCALES WITH AIR COUNT\n      - Total blocks = sum of blocks for each AIR\n      - For each AIR: num_blocks = ceil(num_y / MAX_THREADS_PER_BLOCK)\n      - More AIRs = more blocks, but same grid dimension (num_blocks, num_x)\n   \n   d) INTERMEDIATE BUFFER SIZE: SCALES LINEARLY WITH AIR COUNT\n      - Location: /home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/batch_mle.cu:362\n      - Size = num_x * num_y * buffer_size (per AIR)\n      - Total for batch = sum over all AIRs\n\n6. PERFORMANCE CHARACTERISTICS\n   \n   APC 0 (99 AIRs) -> 119ms total MLE time\n   APC 300 (623 AIRs) -> 164ms total MLE time\n   \n   Ratio: 164/119 = 1.378x slowdown\n   AIR ratio: 623/99 = 6.29x more AIRs\n   \n   NOT LINEAR scaling! Possible reasons:\n   - Reduced memory bandwidth per AIR (more contention)\n   - More kernel launches (overhead)\n   - Cache efficiency drops with more AIRs\n   - Some AIRs may have larger num_y, increasing per-AIR work\n\n7. KEY SCALING FACTORS\n   - Number of MLE rounds: FIXED (only depends on height)\n   - Per-round num_x: FIXED (constraint_degree)\n   - Per-round num_y per AIR: VARIABLE (depends on height and round)\n   - Memory per round: SCALES with sum of (num_y * num_columns) for all AIRs\nEOF\ncat /tmp/summary.txt\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":875,"cache_read_input_tokens":67075,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":875,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01AziaoQyUBvBQHrhM4RkX8Z","session_id":"f245fed0-0457-4d6a-9da2-744553774a6f","uuid":"5c135632-a8cc-4ad6-97b4-628d25baf67f"}
