{"type":"system","subtype":"task_started","task_id":"a2bff906ccc5a37d6","tool_use_id":"toolu_01LHJ2EJ1TiMURYqyPM5soC8","description":"Research MLE degenerate AIR handling","task_type":"local_agent","prompt":"In /home/georg/stark-backend, I need to understand how \"degenerate\" AIRs (those with num_y=1 or height=1 after folding) are handled in the MLE sumcheck rounds.\n\nThe MLE rounds involve batched kernel launches that process all AIRs per round. As rounds progress, smaller AIRs get folded down to height=1. I need to know:\n\n1. In `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`, find the MLE round loop. How does it determine which AIRs to include in each round's batch kernels?\n\n2. Look at `fold_mle_evals` or `fold_pingpong` - what happens to matrices with height=1 after folding? Are they excluded from subsequent GPU kernel processing?\n\n3. In the batch MLE kernel launchers (`batch_mle.rs`), how is the descriptor array built? Does it include AIRs whose matrices have height=1?\n\n4. Look at `sumcheck_polys_batch_eval` or equivalent - does it process ALL AIRs or only active ones?\n\n5. Specifically: after folding reduces an AIR's matrix to height=1, does that AIR still consume GPU blocks in the batch kernels for remaining rounds?\n\nI want to understand whether there's an opportunity to skip \"done\" AIRs in later MLE rounds.\n\nThoroughness: very thorough. Include file paths and line numbers.","uuid":"12ce45ab-e565-4cc7-a015-fe96ed7a9f0b","session_id":"f245fed0-0457-4d6a-9da2-744553774a6f"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"In /home/georg/stark-backend, I need to understand how \"degenerate\" AIRs (those with num_y=1 or height=1 after folding) are handled in the MLE sumcheck rounds.\n\nThe MLE rounds involve batched kernel launches that process all AIRs per round. As rounds progress, smaller AIRs get folded down to height=1. I need to know:\n\n1. In `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`, find the MLE round loop. How does it determine which AIRs to include in each round's batch kernels?\n\n2. Look at `fold_mle_evals` or `fold_pingpong` - what happens to matrices with height=1 after folding? Are they excluded from subsequent GPU kernel processing?\n\n3. In the batch MLE kernel launchers (`batch_mle.rs`), how is the descriptor array built? Does it include AIRs whose matrices have height=1?\n\n4. Look at `sumcheck_polys_batch_eval` or equivalent - does it process ALL AIRs or only active ones?\n\n5. Specifically: after folding reduces an AIR's matrix to height=1, does that AIR still consume GPU blocks in the batch kernels for remaining rounds?\n\nI want to understand whether there's an opportunity to skip \"done\" AIRs in later MLE rounds.\n\nThoroughness: very thorough. Include file paths and line numbers."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01LHJ2EJ1TiMURYqyPM5soC8","session_id":"f245fed0-0457-4d6a-9da2-744553774a6f","uuid":"fadbc090-6345-4460-91b6-75c9311871d7","timestamp":"2026-04-15T15:47:46.742Z"}
