{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_014kMcv36krv5XqW6dZjbJ4K","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a good picture. The current Round 0 code has Phase 1 (build work items) and Phase 2 (multi-stream evaluation). The batch Round 0 code from commit 0d1bb2f9 would fit between Phase 1 and Phase 2 - it identifies batchable AIRs, processes them with batched kernels, and then Phase 2 only handles the remaining (non-batched) AIRs.\n\nLet me now write my optimization ideas, task, and plan. I've done enough research.\n\n**Current Performance Summary:**\n- APC 300 STARK excl trace: 1106ms (2.22x vs 2455ms baseline)\n\n\n- APC 0 STARK excl trace: 1784ms\n- APC 0→300 scaling: 1.61x (target: >2x)\n\n**Optimization Ideas:**\n\n1. **Re-enable batch Round 0 descriptor-array kernels for small AIRs**\n   - Expected impact: 25-40ms on Round 0 at APC 300\n   - Probability: Medium-High (implementation exists in git history, OOM blocker likely resolved)\n   - Complexity: Moderate\n\n2. **Precompute GKR input eval kernel parameters in Phase 1**\n   - Expected impact: 15-20ms on Round 0 at APC 300\n   - Probability: High (straightforward parameter caching)\n   - Complexity: Low\n\n3. **Optimize MLE Round descriptor building by pre-computing Case A/B partition**\n   - Expected impact: 10-15ms on MLE Rounds at APC 300\n   - Probability: Medium (per-round CPU work is ~0.5ms)\n   - Complexity: Simple\n\n4. **Fuse the Round 0 extraction + evaluation into combined kernel**\n   - Expected impact: 10-15ms on Round 0 at APC 300\n   - Probability: Low-Medium (may increase register pressure)\n   - Complexity: Complex\n\n5. **Multi-stream the K2 build + GKR tree operations**\n   - Expected impact: 5-15ms on GKR at APC 300\n   - Probability: Medium (depends on memory bandwidth saturation)\n   - Complexity: Moderate\n\nThe best approach is re-enabling batch Round 0 since it offers the strongest impact-to-effort ratio. The CUDA kernels and Rust orchestration were already designed and tested at APC 0, and the previous blockers around memory and compiler issues have been resolved. I just need to carefully port the original design, implement it cleanly, and verify it works across all APC configurations.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":772,"cache_read_input_tokens":167506,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":772},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f245fed0-0457-4d6a-9da2-744553774a6f","uuid":"acf3f4e5-bf3a-4172-93bd-ff2dee0dbbf5"}
