{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01MmmKHwUXf7tctuE2aqJ9BS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Optimization Ideas\n\n| # | Idea | Expected Impact | Probability | Complexity | Score |\n|---|------|----------------|-------------|------------|-------|\n| 1 | Re-enable batch Round 0 descriptor-array kernels for small AIRs | 25-40ms | Medium-High | Moderate | **High** |\n| 2 | Precompute GKR input eval kernel parameters in Phase 1 | 15-25ms | Medium | Simple-Moderate | Medium |\n| 3 | Pre-compute MLE Round Case A/B partition and descriptors | 10-15ms | Medium | Simple | Medium |\n| 4 | Fuse Round 0 extraction into evaluation kernel | 10-15ms | Low-Medium | Complex | Low |\n| 5 | Multi-stream GKR K2 build operations | 5-15ms | Low | Moderate | Low |\n\n**Selecting Idea #1**: The batch Round 0 path has been implemented 3 times before and consistently blocked by OOM. The OOM was caused by cubin size growth after CUDA rebuilds. The VPMM page size increase (16 MiB) + PRUNE_SHMEM_KERNELS flag have since resolved the memory pressure — I just successfully ran APC 300 at 1106ms on the current build. The batch infrastructure design is proven, and re-enabling it is the highest-impact option."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1106,"cache_read_input_tokens":168278,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1106},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f245fed0-0457-4d6a-9da2-744553774a6f","uuid":"f880c2ad-0ffd-4065-9d14-0cf0e590b4c3"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01MmmKHwUXf7tctuE2aqJ9BS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XS99n6teFWTxkdNJodEVUQ","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md","content":"# 2026-04-15-1800-reenable-batch-round0-small-airs\n\nRe-enable the batch Round 0 descriptor-array kernel path for small AIRs, which was previously implemented (commits 0d1bb2f9, bcb1c0d2) but reverted due to GPU OOM at APC 100/300. The OOM blocker has since been resolved by the VPMM page size increase (16 MiB) and PRUNE_SHMEM_KERNELS, as confirmed by the current successful APC 300 benchmark run (1106ms STARK excl trace). At APC 300, ~250 small coset-parallel AIRs per segment currently require ~1000 individual kernel launches in Round 0; batching them into 2-4 descriptor-array kernel launches is expected to reduce Round 0 from 179ms to ~140-155ms, saving 25-40ms on STARK excl trace.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1106,"cache_read_input_tokens":168278,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1106},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f245fed0-0457-4d6a-9da2-744553774a6f","uuid":"1c74112e-01f2-4589-8ffe-d7bdb8024ae0"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XS99n6teFWTxkdNJodEVUQ","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md has been updated successfully."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f245fed0-0457-4d6a-9da2-744553774a6f","uuid":"fb9c047a-538b-4b31-8fac-19ab8ca79c42","timestamp":"2026-04-15T15:58:07.142Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md","content":"# 2026-04-15-1800-reenable-batch-round0-small-airs\n\nRe-enable the batch Round 0 descriptor-array kernel path for small AIRs, which was previously implemented (commits 0d1bb2f9, bcb1c0d2) but reverted due to GPU OOM at APC 100/300. The OOM blocker has since been resolved by the VPMM page size increase (16 MiB) and PRUNE_SHMEM_KERNELS, as confirmed by the current successful APC 300 benchmark run (1106ms STARK excl trace). At APC 300, ~250 small coset-parallel AIRs per segment currently require ~1000 individual kernel launches in Round 0; batching them into 2-4 descriptor-array kernel launches is expected to reduce Round 0 from 179ms to ~140-155ms, saving 25-40ms on STARK excl trace.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":3,"newStart":1,"newLines":3,"lines":["-# 2026-04-15-1600-fix-batch-round0-revert-and-reapply","+# 2026-04-15-1800-reenable-batch-round0-small-airs"," ","-Revert the broken batch-round0-descriptors commit (0d1bb2f9) which causes APC 300 STARK proving to hang for 12+ minutes, then re-apply the batch Round 0 path with the CPU bottleneck fixed. The existing batch code redundantly reconstructs logup interaction DAGs and rules per batchable AIR via `build_logup_rules_for_air()` (involving `SymbolicDagBuilder`, `SymbolicRulesGpu::new`, and per-AIR device uploads), which takes prohibitively long for the ~300 small AIRs at APC 300. The fix reuses the precomputed `logup_round0_buffer_size` from `AirDataGpu` and the existing per-AIR logup rule data (DAG, rules, weights) that the non-batched path already constructs during Phase 1 work-item preparation, avoiding all redundant CPU-side symbolic computation.","+Re-enable the batch Round 0 descriptor-array kernel path for small AIRs, which was previously implemented (commits 0d1bb2f9, bcb1c0d2) but reverted due to GPU OOM at APC 100/300. The OOM blocker has since been resolved by the VPMM page size increase (16 MiB) and PRUNE_SHMEM_KERNELS, as confirmed by the current successful APC 300 benchmark run (1106ms STARK excl trace). At APC 300, ~250 small coset-parallel AIRs per segment currently require ~1000 individual kernel launches in Round 0; batching them into 2-4 descriptor-array kernel launches is expected to reduce Round 0 from 179ms to ~140-155ms, saving 25-40ms on STARK excl trace."]}],"originalFile":"# 2026-04-15-1600-fix-batch-round0-revert-and-reapply\n\nRevert the broken batch-round0-descriptors commit (0d1bb2f9) which causes APC 300 STARK proving to hang for 12+ minutes, then re-apply the batch Round 0 path with the CPU bottleneck fixed. The existing batch code redundantly reconstructs logup interaction DAGs and rules per batchable AIR via `build_logup_rules_for_air()` (involving `SymbolicDagBuilder`, `SymbolicRulesGpu::new`, and per-AIR device uploads), which takes prohibitively long for the ~300 small AIRs at APC 300. The fix reuses the precomputed `logup_round0_buffer_size` from `AirDataGpu` and the existing per-AIR logup rule data (DAG, rules, weights) that the non-batched path already constructs during Phase 1 work-item preparation, avoiding all redundant CPU-side symbolic computation.\n"}}
