er segment rather than running them sequentially. Checking if the GKR input eval can actually run in parallel with Round 0—it only needs beta, which comes from the transcript after Round 0 finishes, so there's a dependency there that prevents overlap. This means the 74ms savings I calculated wouldn't actually materialize since GKR input eval is blocked waiting for Round 0's output. The GKR input evaluation actually depends on the final evaluation points from the MLE Rounds, not Round 0 directly, so GKR runs after MLE completes. Looking at the timing breakdown where LogUp GKR takes 361ms, Round 0 takes 179ms, and MLE Rounds takes 164ms—these add up to the total Constraints time, so I need to check the actual code to determine the execution order rather than relying on the spec output listing.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3139,"cache_read_input_tokens":180275,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3139},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f245fed0-0457-4d6a-9da2-744553774a6f","uuid":"b75c9478-2c34-4df0-a79a-2ea724d09ba5"}
