{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FKwHAjKXYmyXsEVrdswonj","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Plan: Re-enable Batch Round 0 Descriptor-Array Kernels for Small AIRs\n2\t\n3\t## Goal\n4\t\n5\tReduce Round 0 wall-clock time at APC 300 by batching the ~250 small coset-parallel AIRs per segment. The batch path runs eval+extraction on the default CUDA stream before the multi-threaded Phase 2, which then only processes the remaining ~60 large AIRs. This eliminates ~500 eval kernel launches per segment and moves ~250 AIRs' CPU overhead (SymbolicConstraints::from, rule building) out of the multi-threaded critical path.\n6\t\n7\tCurrent: Round 0 = 179ms (90ms/seg). Expected after: Round 0 = 120-145ms (60-73ms/seg). Net savings: 35-60ms on STARK excl trace (1106ms → 1046-1071ms).\n8\t\n9\tPrevious implementations (commits `0c699f47`, `bcb1c0d2`, `0d1bb2f9`) were reverted due to GPU OOM at APC 100/300. The OOM has since been resolved (VPMM 16 MiB page size + PRUNE_SHMEM_KERNELS), confirmed by the current APC 300 run at 1106ms.\n10\t\n11\t## Current Code Path\n12\t\n13\t**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n14\t\n15\t### Phase 1 (single-threaded, lines 1022-1198)\n16\tBuilds `Vec<Round0AirWorkItem>` for all AIRs. Each work item has: proving key refs, trace pointers, pre-computed buffer sizes, eq_3bs, `Round0ExtractTables`. Items sorted by descending height. Percentile buffer sizes computed for pre-allocation.\n17\t\n18\t### Phase 1.5 (overlapped background, lines 1341-1393)\n19\tBackground thread uploads `d_eq_3b_per_trace` and precomputes `logup_combinations`, concurrent with Phase 2.\n20\t\n21\t### Phase 2 (multi-threaded, lines 1319-1413)\n22\t8 OS threads, per-thread CUDA streams, round-robin assignment. Per AIR: `process_air_round0()` does:\n23\t1. `evaluate_round0_zerocheck_gpu()` → zerocheck eval + reduction\n24\t2. `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu()` → calls `SymbolicConstraints::from()`, builds DAG, encodes rules, H2D uploads, logup eval + reduction\n25\t3. `_round0_extract_zerocheck_poly()` → GPU extraction to `d_batch_array`\n26\t4. `_round0_extract_logup_polys()` → GPU extraction to `d_batch_array`\n27\t\n28\tAt APC 300: ~312 AIRs/seg, ~4 kernel launches/AIR = ~1248 eval+extraction launches/seg. Wall clock: ~90ms/seg.\n29\t\n30\t### Why it's slow at APC 300\n31\tPhase 2 processes ~312 AIRs across 8 threads (~39/thread). For the ~250 small AIRs (height ≤ 256), each one has:\n32\t- CPU cost: `SymbolicConstraints::from()` (~0.1ms) + DAG build + rule encode in `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu()` (~0.1ms)\n33\t- GPU eval time: ~50-200μs (tiny, GPU-underutilized)\n34\t- 4 kernel launches with ~10μs overhead each\n35\t\n36\tThe per-AIR CPU work (~0.2ms) dominates over GPU compute for small AIRs. 250 small AIRs × 0.2ms / 8 threads ≈ 6ms of serialized CPU overhead per thread. The GPU eval of these small AIRs takes ~4ms/thread but is interleaved with large AIRs.\n37\t\n38\t## Changes\n39\t\n40\t### Change 0: Diagnose the previous GPU hang\n41\t\n42\t**Before any code changes**, run the reverted batch Round 0 kernels from commit `0d1bb2f9` under `compute-sanitizer --tool memcheck` to identify whether the 12-minute hang at APC 300 (reported in the 1600 report) was caused by an out-of-bounds memory access, infinite loop, or other bug. Steps:\n43\t1. Cherry-pick `0d1bb2f9` onto a throwaway branch\n44\t2. Build with debug symbols\n45\t3. Run: `compute-sanitizer --tool memcheck -- $PROVE_BIN prove --artifact apc300.cbor --input 0 --recursion`\n46\t4. If memcheck identifies an OOB access: fix the specific bug in the new implementation\n47\t5. If memcheck shows no errors: the hang was likely caused by the OOM (now resolved) or by the Rust optimizer issue (fixed by `#[inline(never)]`)\n48\t6. Revert the cherry-pick before proceeding\n49\t\n50\tThis step de-risks the CUDA kernel code before investing in the Rust orchestration.\n51\t\n52\t### Change 1: Store logup Round 0 rules in proving key at keygen time\n53\t\n54\t**Files:**\n55\t- `crates/cuda-backend/src/pkey.rs`\n56\t\n57\tAdd a `LogupRound0Rules` struct to `AirDataGpu` containing the encoded logup DAG rules + interaction-to-rule-index mapping + per-challenge weight vectors. This is the same keygen-time pre-computation from commit `5bec2ee1` (reverted `52873be4`), but the stored rules are used **ONLY by the batch path** (Change 3), NOT by Phase 2. Phase 2 continues to reconstruct rules per-AIR as before, preserving the beneficial GPU pacing.\n58\t\n59\tThe `logup_round0_buffer_size` field is already present in `AirDataGpu` (added by the `prealloc-round0-threshold-buffers` task). This change adds the full rules alongside it.\n60\t\n61\t**Why this doesn't regress like commit 5bec2ee1:** That commit modified Phase 2's `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu` to use keygen-time rules, removing the per-AIR CPU work that served as GPU pacing. This change does NOT modify Phase 2 at all — Phase 2 is unchanged. The keygen rules are only consumed by the new `batch_round0_small_airs` function (Change 3).\n62\t\n63\t### Change 2: CUDA Batched Kernels\n64\t\n65\t**Files:**\n66\t- `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/zerocheck_round0.cu`\n67\t- `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/logup_round0.cu`\n68\t\n69\tReplicate the descriptor-array kernel design from reverted commit `0d1bb2f9`:\n70\t\n71\t- **`batched_zerocheck_r0_coset_parallel_kernel`**: Block-to-AIR mapping via `Round0BlockCtx` array. Each `Round0ZcCtx` descriptor has all per-AIR parameters. Only `GLOBAL=true, NEEDS_SHMEM=false` instantiation (PRUNE_SHMEM_KERNELS active). Uses the existing single-AIR kernel body, wrapped with a descriptor lookup preamble.\n72\t\n73\t- **`batched_logup_r0_coset_parallel_kernel`**: Same pattern with `Round0LogupCtx` descriptors. Uses keygen-time pre-computed rules (device pointers from Change 1).\n74\t\n75\t- **`batched_final_reduce_block_sums`**: Reuse the existing reduction pattern from `batch_mle.cu`.\n76\t\n77\t**Null intermediates:** For AIRs with `zc_intermed_cap == 0` (no zerocheck constraints) or `logup_intermed_cap == 0`, the descriptor's intermediates pointer is set to a valid offset in the arena (pointing past all used data). The kernel code already guards against `buffer_size == 0` by skipping the intermediates write path. The previous `cudaErrorIllegalAddress` (from commit `0c699f47`) occurred because GLOBAL-mode kernels unconditionally dereferenced intermediates for all blocks — the batched kernel must check `buffer_size > 0` before writing to intermediates, or the null descriptor must be excluded from the launch.\n78\t\n79\t### Change 3: FFI Bindings\n80\t\n81\t**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs`\n82\t\n83\tAdd `#[repr(C)]` Rust structs mirroring the CUDA descriptors:\n84\t- `Round0BlockCtx { air_idx: u32, local_block_idx_x: u32 }`\n85\t- `Round0ZcCtx` with fields: main_trace_ptr, preprocessed_ptr, buffer_size, num_x, skip_domain, num_cosets, eq_xis_ptr, sels_ptr, output_ptr, output_offset\n86\t- `Round0LogupCtx` with fields: trace ptrs, encoded_rules_ptr, rules_len, weight ptrs, buffer_size, eq_3b_ptr, output_ptr, output_offset\n87\t\n88\tAdd extern \"C\" declarations and safe wrappers.\n89\t\n90\t### Change 4: Batch Orchestration Module\n91\t\n92\t**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0_batched.rs` (new file)\n93\t\n94\tAll public functions `#[inline(never)]` to prevent Rust optimizer interference.\n95\t\n96\t**`identify_batchable_airs(work_items, l_skip) -> Vec<bool>`**\n97\t- Batchable if: (a) coset-parallel (`num_x * skip_domain < 32768`), (b) intermediates within budget (`< 16M Fp`), (c) AIR has zerocheck OR logup work\n98\t- Returns all-false if fewer than 50 qualify (disabled at APC 0 with ~20 AIRs/seg)\n99\t\n100\t**`batch_round0_small_airs(work_items, batch_mask, pk, extract_tables, d_batch_ptr, ...) -> Result<()>`**\n101\t1. Group batchable AIRs by `num_cosets_zc` (constraint_degree − 1) — AIRs with different num_cosets need separate launches.\n102\t2. For each group:\n103\t   a. Compute total intermediates size (sum of per-AIR sizes) and allocate shared arena `DeviceBuffer`\n104\t   b. Build `Round0ZcCtx` descriptors: use proving key pointers (trace, preprocessed, zerocheck config) and arena offsets for intermediates. Output offsets point into `d_batch_array` at each AIR's `trace_idx`.\n105\t   c. Build `Round0BlockCtx` mapping array\n106\t   d. Upload descriptors + block_ctxs to GPU\n107\t   e. Launch `batched_zerocheck_r0_coset_parallel_kernel` + reduction\n108\t   f. Build `Round0LogupCtx` descriptors: use keygen-time logup rules from `pk.per_air[air_idx].other_data.logup_round0_rules` (Change 1). Compute per-challenge interaction weights from current `beta_pows` and `eq_3bs`.\n109\t   g. Launch `batched_logup_r0_coset_parallel_kernel` + reduction\n110\t   h. For each batched AIR: call `_round0_extract_zerocheck_poly()` and `_round0_extract_logup_polys()` to write final polynomial coefficients into `d_batch_array`\n111\t3. Sync default stream\n112\t\n113\t**Per-AIR extraction (step 2h):** The ~500 extraction launches (250 AIRs × 2) add ~25ms on the default stream. This is the largest cost in the batch path. A future iteration could batch extraction too, but per-AIR extraction is simpler, uses the proven existing kernels, and keeps this change more manageable.\n114\t\n115\t**Per-AIR interaction weight computation (step 2f):** Computing interaction weights requires current `beta_pows` and `eq_3bs` values (challenge-dependent, can't be pre-computed at keygen). This is ~10μs per AIR of CPU arithmetic. For 250 AIRs: 2.5ms. Not a significant cost.\n116\t\n117\t### Change 5: Integration\n118\t\n119\t**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n120\t\n121\tInsert the batch path between Phase 1 and the `num_threads` branching point (line 1208). The batch path runs only in the multi-threaded case (`num_threads > 1`, i.e., APC 100/300 with ≥100 AIRs). In the single-threaded case (`num_threads <= 1`, APC 0), the batch path is skipped because `identify_batchable_airs` returns all-false (< 50 qualifying AIRs).\n122\t\n123\t```rust\n124\t// After Phase 1 (work items + extract tables built, d_batch_array allocated, sync done)\n125\tlet batch_mask = round0_batched::identify_batchable_airs(&work_items, l_skip);\n126\tlet has_batched = batch_mask.iter().any(|&b| b);\n127\tif has_batched {\n128\t    round0_batched::batch_round0_small_airs(\n129\t        &work_items, &batch_mask, self.pk, &extract_tables,\n130\t        d_batch_array.as_mut_ptr(), l_skip,\n131\t        &self.eq_3b_per_trace, &self.beta_pows,\n132\t    )?;\n133\t    // batch writes to d_batch_array on default stream; sync before worker threads start\n134\t    current_stream_sync()?;\n135\t}\n136\t```\n137\t\n138\tIn Phase 2, the worker threads skip batched AIRs:\n139\t```rust\n140\tfor &item_idx in &thread_items[thread_id] {\n141\t    if batch_mask[item_idx] { continue; }\n142\t    process_air_round0(&work_items[item_idx], &mut bufs, batch_ptr_val as *mut EF, &extract_tables)?;\n143\t}\n144\t```\n145\t\n146\t### Change 6: Visibility\n147\t\n148\t**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n149\t\n150\tWiden `Round0AirWorkItem` and `Round0ExtractTables` to `pub(super)` or place `round0_batched.rs` as a submodule of `logup_zerocheck` so it has access.\n151\t\n152\t## Invariants\n153\t\n154\t1. **Correctness**: Batched eval produces the same coset-parallel NTT + constraint evaluation as per-AIR eval. Extraction uses the identical per-AIR kernels, writing to the same `d_batch_array` offsets.\n155\t\n156\t2. **APC 0 guard**: `MIN_BATCHABLE_AIRS = 50` disables batching at APC 0 (≤20 AIRs/seg). The single-threaded path (`num_threads <= 1`) is completely unchanged.\n157\t\n158\t3. **Phase 2 pacing preserved**: Phase 2's `process_air_round0` is unchanged for non-batched AIRs. The per-AIR `SymbolicConstraints::from()` + rule building remains as GPU pacing for large AIRs. Phase 2 does NOT use the keygen-time logup rules.\n159\t\n160\t4. **Stream ordering**: Batch path on default stream → `current_stream_sync()` → Phase 2 on per-thread streams. Batch results visible to all worker threads. Phase 2 results joined at scope exit.\n161\t\n162\t5. **Memory**: Shared intermediates arena sized by summing per-AIR needs. Typical size: 10-50MB for ~250 small AIRs (well within L2 cache). Per-AIR budget cap (16M Fp ≈ 64MB) prevents outliers from inflating the arena.\n163\t\n164\t6. **Null pointer safety**: Descriptors for AIRs with `buffer_size == 0` (no intermediates needed) get the arena base pointer as intermediates. The kernel checks `buffer_size > 0` before writing to intermediates. This avoids the `cudaErrorIllegalAddress` from the original attempt.\n165\t\n166\t## Measurement Plan\n167\t\n168\t1. **Step 0**: Run `compute-sanitizer --tool memcheck` on cherry-picked `0d1bb2f9` to diagnose the previous GPU hang (see Change 0)\n169\t2. Build: `cd /home/georg/powdr && cargo build --bin powdr_openvm_riscv -r --features \"metrics,cuda\"`\n170\t3. APC 0 regression: verify Round 0 ≤ 180ms, STARK excl trace ≤ 1810ms\n171\t4. APC 300: expect Round 0 120-145ms (from 179ms), STARK excl trace 1046-1071ms\n172\t5. APC 100 for completeness\n173\t6. If APC 300 passes but Round 0 savings < 25ms: profile batch path overhead with tracing spans to identify whether descriptor building, extraction, or eval dominates\n174\t\n175\t## Rollback Criteria\n176\t\n177\t- **Hard revert**: APC 0 STARK excl trace regresses >20ms vs 1784ms\n178\t- **Hard revert**: Verification failure at any APC config\n179\t- **Hard revert**: GPU OOM, `cudaErrorIllegalAddress`, or GPU hang at any APC config\n180\t- **Soft revert**: APC 300 Round 0 improvement <10ms\n181\t- **Soft revert**: APC 300 STARK excl trace improvement <20ms\n182\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_016YMbBdxr7jKnQmakTAbjjJ","session_id":"f245fed0-0457-4d6a-9da2-744553774a6f","uuid":"2464f463-2d68-4a2e-bfe6-d431da049e7e","timestamp":"2026-04-15T16:09:15.038Z"}
