{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01P7BD273h28TKVKdHNL6cRL","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t## Goal\n2\t\n3\tFix the batch Round 0 descriptor-array optimization so it works at APC 300 without the 12+ minute regression introduced by commit 0d1bb2f9. Round 0 is the worst-scaling component of STARK excl trace: 177ms at APC 0 vs 187ms at APC 300 (0.95x, no scaling despite 2.35x fewer cells). The batched approach eliminates ~500 per-AIR kernel launches for small AIRs while preserving the multi-stream path for large AIRs. Expected improvement: 5-15ms on Round 0 at APC 300, primarily from eliminating per-AIR kernel launch and H2D overhead for small AIRs, with possible additional GPU occupancy benefits from batched execution.\n4\t\n5\t## Current Code Path\n6\t\n7\t### Round 0 evaluation flow (mod.rs, `sumcheck_uni_round0_polys`)\n8\t\n9\t1. **Phase 1** (single-threaded, lines 900-1190): Build work items, compute eq_xis, prepare selectors, allocate d_batch_array.\n10\t\n11\t2. **Phase 1b** (single-threaded, lines 1194-1210): The batch path from commit 0d1bb2f9:\n12\t   - `identify_batchable_airs()` (round0_batched.rs:42) — marks AIRs with coset-parallel mode and intermediates < 16M Fp as batchable; requires >= 50 qualifying AIRs.\n13\t   - `batch_round0_small_airs()` (round0_batched.rs:192) — for each batchable AIR, calls `build_logup_rules_for_air()` (round0_batched.rs:96), which:\n14\t     - Calls `SymbolicConstraints::from(&single_pk.vk.symbolic_constraints)` to convert compact VK representation to full expression trees\n15\t     - Builds a `SymbolicDagBuilder` and DAG\n16\t     - Creates `SymbolicRulesGpu::new(&dag, true)` — computes rules and buffer sizes\n17\t     - Computes numer/denom weights\n18\t     - Uploads rules and weights to GPU (3 H2D transfers per AIR)\n19\t   - Groups by num_cosets, launches batched zerocheck and logup kernels\n20\t   - Runs per-AIR extraction (writes to d_batch_array via GPU kernels)\n21\t\n22\t3. **Phase 2** (multi-threaded, lines 1212-1400): For each non-batchable AIR, calls `process_air_round0()` (mod.rs:234), which:\n23\t   - Also calls `SymbolicConstraints::from()` per AIR (line 241) — this is needed for both zerocheck (via `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu`) and logup (via `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu`)\n24\t   - Builds logup DAG and rules in `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu()` (round0.rs:162)\n25\t   - Launches per-AIR zerocheck + logup kernels\n26\t   - Runs per-AIR GPU extraction\n27\t\n28\t### Root cause of the regression\n29\t\n30\tThe 12+ minute APC 300 hang has two possible causes, which must be disambiguated:"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_016YMbBdxr7jKnQmakTAbjjJ","session_id":"f245fed0-0457-4d6a-9da2-744553774a6f","uuid":"939a5858-b384-4437-a890-52e04f0469ee","timestamp":"2026-04-15T16:10:05.275Z"}
