{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01V3nTnkyYdBBCUZsYcjrmzh","type":"tool_result","content":"0\t# Plan: Re-enable Batch Round 0 Descriptor-Array Kernels for Small AIRs\n1\t\n2\t## Goal\n3\t\n4\tReduce Round 0 wall-clock time at APC 300 by batching the ~250 small coset-parallel AIRs per segment. The batch path runs eval+extraction on the default CUDA stream before the multi-threaded Phase 2, which then only processes the remaining ~60 large AIRs. This eliminates ~500 eval kernel launches per segment and moves ~250 AIRs' CPU overhead (SymbolicConstraints::from, rule building) out of the multi-threaded critical path.\n5\t\n6\tCurrent: Round 0 = 179ms (90ms/seg). Expected after: Round 0 = 120-145ms (60-73ms/seg). Net savings: 35-60ms on STARK excl trace (1106ms → 1046-1071ms).\n7\t\n8\tPrevious implementations (commits `0c699f47`, `bcb1c0d2`, `0d1bb2f9`) were reverted due to GPU OOM at APC 100/300. The OOM has since been resolved (VPMM 16 MiB page size + PRUNE_SHMEM_KERNELS), confirmed by the current APC 300 run at 1106ms.\n9\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f245fed0-0457-4d6a-9da2-744553774a6f","uuid":"44da3636-8e0d-49c7-baf7-4a509682dd8d","timestamp":"2026-04-15T16:14:01.930Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-15-1800-reenable-batch-round0-small-airs/plan.md","content":"# Plan: Re-enable Batch Round 0 Descriptor-Array Kernels for Small AIRs\n\n## Goal\n\nReduce Round 0 wall-clock time at APC 300 by batching the ~250 small coset-parallel AIRs per segment. The batch path runs eval+extraction on the default CUDA stream before the multi-threaded Phase 2, which then only processes the remaining ~60 large AIRs. This eliminates ~500 eval kernel launches per segment and moves ~250 AIRs' CPU overhead (SymbolicConstraints::from, rule building) out of the multi-threaded critical path.\n\nCurrent: Round 0 = 179ms (90ms/seg). Expected after: Round 0 = 120-145ms (60-73ms/seg). Net savings: 35-60ms on STARK excl trace (1106ms → 1046-1071ms).\n\nPrevious implementations (commits `0c699f47`, `bcb1c0d2`, `0d1bb2f9`) were reverted due to GPU OOM at APC 100/300. The OOM has since been resolved (VPMM 16 MiB page size + PRUNE_SHMEM_KERNELS), confirmed by the current APC 300 run at 1106ms.\n","numLines":10,"startLine":0,"totalLines":182}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Gd373SDC2WGDov8ajEE6RN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012g2C5AXq4goYoFJszB7fjX","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-15-1800-reenable-batch-round0-small-airs/plan.md","content":"# Plan: Re-enable Batch Round 0 Descriptor-Array Kernels for Small AIRs\n\n## Goal\n\nReduce Round 0 wall-clock time at APC 300 by batching the eval kernels for ~250 small coset-parallel AIRs per segment into 2-4 descriptor-array kernel launches on the default stream, then letting Phase 2 worker threads handle extraction for batched AIRs alongside full processing of the remaining ~60 large AIRs. This eliminates ~500 eval kernel launches per segment plus the per-AIR CPU overhead (`SymbolicConstraints::from`, DAG build, rule encode) for batched AIRs, without serializing extraction onto the critical path.\n\nCurrent: Round 0 = 179ms (90ms/seg). Expected after: Round 0 = 145-165ms (73-83ms/seg). Estimated net savings: 15-35ms on STARK excl trace (1106ms → 1071-1091ms).\n\nPrevious implementations (commits `0c699f47`, `bcb1c0d2`, `0d1bb2f9`) were reverted due to GPU OOM at APC 100/300. The OOM has since been resolved (VPMM 16 MiB page size + PRUNE_SHMEM_KERNELS), confirmed by the current APC 300 run at 1106ms.\n\n## Current Code Path\n\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n\n### Phase 1 (single-threaded, lines 1022-1198)\nBuilds `Vec<Round0AirWorkItem>` for all AIRs with proving key refs, trace pointers, pre-computed buffer sizes, eq_3bs, and `Round0ExtractTables`. Items sorted by descending height. Percentile buffer sizes computed for per-thread pre-allocation.\n\n### Phase 1.5 (overlapped background, lines 1341-1382)\nBackground thread uploads `d_eq_3b_per_trace` and precomputes `logup_combinations`, concurrent with Phase 2.\n\n### Phase 2 (multi-threaded, lines 1319-1413)\n8 OS threads, per-thread CUDA streams, round-robin assignment. Per AIR: `process_air_round0()` at `round0.rs` does:\n1. `evaluate_round0_zerocheck_gpu()` → zerocheck eval + reduction (~2 kernel launches)\n2. `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu()` → CPU rule construction (`SymbolicConstraints::from`, DAG, encode, H2D) + logup eval + reduction (~2 kernel launches)\n3. `_round0_extract_zerocheck_poly()` → GPU extraction to `d_batch_array` (1 kernel launch)\n4. `_round0_extract_logup_polys()` → GPU extraction to `d_batch_array` (1 kernel launch)\n\nAt APC 300: ~312 AIRs/seg, ~6 kernel launches/AIR = ~1872 launches/seg. Wall clock: ~90ms/seg.\n\n### Why it's slow at APC 300\nThe ~250 small AIRs (coset-parallel, height ≤ 256) each take ~0.2ms CPU work + ~0.1ms GPU eval + ~0.1ms extraction = ~0.4ms total. Across 8 threads: 31 per thread × 0.4ms ≈ 12ms. The remaining ~60 large AIRs take ~3-10ms each, ~8 per thread, total ~24-40ms. But measured per-segment Round 0 is ~90ms, with the difference attributable to CUDA driver overhead, stream scheduling, and memory pool contention across 1872 kernel launches.\n\n## Changes\n\n### Change 0: Diagnose the previous GPU hang\n\n**Before any code changes**, reproduce and diagnose the 12-minute GPU hang from commit `0d1bb2f9`:\n1. Cherry-pick `0d1bb2f9` onto a throwaway branch\n2. Build with debug symbols\n3. Run: `compute-sanitizer --tool memcheck -- $PROVE_BIN prove --artifact apc300.cbor --input 0 --recursion`\n4. If memcheck identifies an OOB access: note the location and fix in the new implementation\n5. If no memcheck error: the hang was likely caused by the OOM (now resolved) — this de-risks the approach\n6. Revert the cherry-pick\n\n### Change 1: Store logup Round 0 rules in proving key at keygen time\n\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/pkey.rs`\n\nAdd a `LogupRound0Rules` struct to `AirDataGpu` containing challenge-independent data only:\n- `d_rules: DeviceBuffer<u128>` — encoded DAG rules on GPU\n- `rules_len: usize` — number of rules\n- `buffer_size: u32` — logup intermediates buffer size (already present as `logup_round0_buffer_size`)\n- `dag_idx_to_rule_idx: Vec<usize>` — mapping from interaction index to rule index\n\n**NOT included** (challenge-dependent, computed per-proof):\n- Interaction weight vectors (`numer_weights`, `denom_weights`, `denom_sum_init`) — these depend on `beta_pows` and `eq_3bs` and must be computed at proving time\n\nThese rules are used **ONLY by the batch path** (Change 4). Phase 2's `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu` is unchanged and continues to reconstruct rules per-AIR, preserving the GPU pacing.\n\n### Change 2: CUDA Batched Kernels\n\n**Files:**\n- `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/zerocheck_round0.cu`\n- `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/logup_round0.cu`\n\nReplicate the descriptor-array kernel design from reverted commit `0d1bb2f9`:\n\n- **`batched_zerocheck_r0_coset_parallel_kernel`**: Block-to-AIR mapping via `Round0BlockCtx` array. Each `Round0ZcCtx` descriptor has per-AIR parameters (main/preprocessed pointers, constraint config, eq_xis, sels, intermediates offset, output offset). Only `GLOBAL=true, NEEDS_SHMEM=false` instantiation. Uses the existing single-AIR kernel body with a descriptor lookup preamble.\n\n- **`batched_logup_r0_coset_parallel_kernel`**: Same pattern with `Round0LogupCtx` descriptors. Uses keygen-time rules from Change 1 (device pointers in descriptor) plus proving-time interaction weights (computed in Change 4).\n\n- **`batched_final_reduce_block_sums`**: Reuse the existing reduction pattern from `batch_mle.cu`.\n\n**Null intermediates safety:** Descriptors for AIRs with `buffer_size == 0` get the arena base pointer as their intermediates pointer. The kernel guards intermediates writes with `if (buffer_size > 0)`. The `cudaErrorIllegalAddress` from commit `0c699f47` was caused by unconditional intermediates dereference; this guard prevents it.\n\n### Change 3: FFI Bindings\n\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs`\n\nAdd `#[repr(C)]` Rust structs:\n- `Round0BlockCtx { air_idx: u32, local_block_idx_x: u32 }`\n- `Round0ZcCtx` — main_trace_ptr, preprocessed_ptr, buffer_size, num_x, skip_domain, num_cosets, eq_xis_ptr, sels_ptr, intermediates_offset, output_offset\n- `Round0LogupCtx` — trace ptrs, d_rules_ptr, rules_len, d_numer_weights_ptr, d_denom_weights_ptr, buffer_size, d_eq_3b_ptr, intermediates_offset, output_offset\n\nAdd extern \"C\" declarations and safe Rust wrappers.\n\n### Change 4: Batch Orchestration Module\n\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0_batched.rs` (new file)\n\nAll public functions `#[inline(never)]`.\n\n**`identify_batchable_airs(work_items, l_skip) -> Vec<bool>`**\n- Batchable if: (a) coset-parallel (`num_x * skip_domain < 32768`), (b) intermediates within budget (`< 16M Fp` per AIR), (c) AIR has zerocheck constraints or logup interactions\n- Returns all-false if fewer than `MIN_BATCHABLE_AIRS = 50` qualify\n- **Also** computes and logs the aggregate intermediates size for the reviewer's L2 cache concern: `info!(\"Batch Round 0: {} AIRs, aggregate intermediates: {} MB\", count, total_bytes / 1_000_000)`\n\n**`batch_round0_eval_only(work_items, batch_mask, pk, d_batch_ptr, ...) -> Result<BatchEvalState>`**\nThis function runs on the default stream and performs **only the eval kernels**, NOT extraction. Returns a `BatchEvalState` containing per-AIR result pointers and metadata needed for extraction.\n\nSteps:\n1. Group batchable AIRs by `num_cosets_zc` (constraint_degree − 1)\n2. For each group:\n   a. Compute total intermediates size (sum of per-AIR `zc_intermed_cap + logup_intermed_cap`)\n   b. Allocate shared intermediates arena `DeviceBuffer`\n   c. Build `Round0ZcCtx` descriptors with arena offsets\n   d. Build `Round0BlockCtx` mapping\n   e. Upload descriptors to GPU\n   f. Launch `batched_zerocheck_r0_coset_parallel_kernel` + reduction\n   g. Compute proving-time interaction weights per AIR (CPU: ~10μs/AIR using `beta_pows` and `eq_3bs`)\n   h. Upload `d_numer_weights`, `d_denom_weights` to GPU\n   i. Build `Round0LogupCtx` descriptors using keygen-time rules from `pk.per_air[air_idx].other_data.logup_round0_rules`\n   j. Launch `batched_logup_r0_coset_parallel_kernel` + reduction\n3. Return `BatchEvalState` with per-AIR eval result offsets into the intermediates arena\n\n**Key design: extraction is NOT done here.** Extraction is deferred to Phase 2 worker threads (Change 5).\n\n### Change 5: Integration\n\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n\nInsert the batch eval between Phase 1 (after `current_stream_sync()` at line 1202) and the `num_threads` branch:\n\n```rust\n// Batch eval for small AIRs (default stream)\nlet batch_mask = round0_batched::identify_batchable_airs(&work_items, l_skip);\nlet batch_eval_state = if batch_mask.iter().any(|&b| b) {\n    let state = round0_batched::batch_round0_eval_only(\n        &work_items, &batch_mask, self.pk,\n        d_batch_array.as_mut_ptr(), l_skip,\n        &self.eq_3b_per_trace, &self.beta_pows,\n    )?;\n    current_stream_sync()?; // batch eval results visible to all streams\n    Some(state)\n} else {\n    None\n};\n```\n\nIn Phase 2 worker threads, handle batched AIRs with extraction-only:\n```rust\nfor &item_idx in &thread_items[thread_id] {\n    if batch_mask[item_idx] {\n        // Batch eval already done; only run extraction\n        let w = &work_items[item_idx];\n        round0_batched::extract_batched_air(\n            w, &batch_eval_state.as_ref().unwrap(),\n            batch_ptr_val as *mut EF, &extract_tables,\n        )?;\n    } else {\n        // Full per-AIR processing (eval + extraction, unchanged)\n        process_air_round0(&work_items[item_idx], &mut bufs, batch_ptr_val as *mut EF, &extract_tables)?;\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**Single-threaded path** (`num_threads <= 1`, lines 1280-1318): The batch path is skipped because `identify_batchable_airs` returns all-false (< 50 AIRs at APC 0). If somehow triggered, the single-threaded path would also check `batch_mask` — but this is a no-op since the mask is all-false.\n\n### Change 6: Visibility\n\nWiden `Round0AirWorkItem` and `Round0ExtractTables` to `pub(super)` and place `round0_batched.rs` as a submodule of `logup_zerocheck`.\n\n## Savings Breakdown (per segment at APC 300)\n\n| Component | Current | After | Change | Source |\n|-----------|---------|-------|--------|--------|\n| Batch eval (default stream) | 0ms | 5-8ms | +5-8ms | New: descriptor build + batched kernel |\n| Small AIR CPU work in Phase 2 | ~6ms/thread | 0ms | −6ms | Eliminated: skip SymbolicConstraints::from, rule build |\n| Small AIR eval launches in Phase 2 | ~5ms/thread | 0ms | −5ms | Eliminated: ~31 AIRs × 6 launches × 10μs |\n| Small AIR extraction in Phase 2 | ~3ms/thread | ~3ms/thread | 0ms | Unchanged: extraction runs on worker threads |\n| Large AIR processing in Phase 2 | ~40ms (max thread) | ~40ms (max thread) | 0ms | Unchanged |\n| CUDA overhead (scheduling, pool) | ~36ms | ~20-30ms | −6-16ms | Fewer kernel launches = less driver overhead |\n| **Total per segment** | **~90ms** | **~68-81ms** | **−9-22ms** | |\n| **Total (2 segments)** | **179ms** | **135-162ms** | **17-44ms** | |\n\nThe improvement is driven by: (1) eliminating ~11ms/thread of small-AIR CPU+launch overhead, and (2) reducing systemic CUDA driver overhead from fewer total kernel launches (~1872 → ~1372 per segment, a 27% reduction).\n\n## Invariants\n\n1. **Correctness**: Batched eval produces the same coset-parallel NTT + constraint evaluation as per-AIR eval. Extraction uses the identical per-AIR kernels and writes to the same `d_batch_array` offsets.\n\n2. **APC 0 guard**: `MIN_BATCHABLE_AIRS = 50` disables batching (APC 0 has ~20 AIRs/seg).\n\n3. **Phase 2 pacing preserved**: Phase 2 is unchanged for non-batched (large) AIRs. Per-AIR `SymbolicConstraints::from()` + rule building remain as GPU pacing for large AIRs.\n\n4. **Stream ordering**: Batch eval on default stream → `current_stream_sync()` → Phase 2 on per-thread streams. Batch eval results are visible before any extraction runs.\n\n5. **Extraction concurrency preserved**: Extraction for batched AIRs runs on Phase 2 worker threads (not the default stream), maintaining 8-way concurrent extraction just like the current code.\n\n6. **L2 cache budget**: The aggregate intermediates arena for ~250 small AIRs is logged at runtime. Expected size: 10-50MB (well within 72MB L2). If > 72MB, the L2 thrashing documented in `batch-global-gkr-input-eval` would apply and we'd see a regression — caught by measurement.\n\n7. **Null pointer safety**: Descriptors with `buffer_size == 0` get arena base pointer + kernel guards writes with `if (buffer_size > 0)`.\n\n## Measurement Plan\n\n1. **Step 0**: Run `compute-sanitizer --tool memcheck` on cherry-picked `0d1bb2f9` at APC 300\n2. Build: `cd /home/georg/powdr && cargo build --bin powdr_openvm_riscv -r --features \"metrics,cuda\"`\n3. APC 0: verify Round 0 ≤ 180ms, STARK excl trace ≤ 1810ms\n4. APC 300: expect Round 0 135-162ms (from 179ms), STARK excl trace 1062-1089ms\n5. APC 100 for completeness\n6. If Round 0 savings < 10ms: add tracing spans inside `batch_round0_eval_only` to identify bottleneck (descriptor build vs eval vs weight computation)\n\n## Rollback Criteria\n\n- **Hard revert**: APC 0 STARK excl trace regresses >20ms vs 1784ms\n- **Hard revert**: Verification failure at any APC config\n- **Hard revert**: GPU OOM, `cudaErrorIllegalAddress`, or GPU hang at any APC config\n- **Soft revert**: APC 300 Round 0 improvement <10ms\n- **Soft revert**: APC 300 STARK excl trace improvement <15ms\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2189,"cache_read_input_tokens":209966,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2189},"output_tokens":65,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f245fed0-0457-4d6a-9da2-744553774a6f","uuid":"07994861-dff0-4bfd-a8ca-e1ac918a6c12"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012g2C5AXq4goYoFJszB7fjX","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-15-1800-reenable-batch-round0-small-airs/plan.md has been updated successfully."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f245fed0-0457-4d6a-9da2-744553774a6f","uuid":"42a13304-301f-4974-8380-f122ae18605e","timestamp":"2026-04-15T16:15:36.007Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-15-1800-reenable-batch-round0-small-airs/plan.md","content":"# Plan: Re-enable Batch Round 0 Descriptor-Array Kernels for Small AIRs\n\n## Goal\n\nReduce Round 0 wall-clock time at APC 300 by batching the eval kernels for ~250 small coset-parallel AIRs per segment into 2-4 descriptor-array kernel launches on the default stream, then letting Phase 2 worker threads handle extraction for batched AIRs alongside full processing of the remaining ~60 large AIRs. This eliminates ~500 eval kernel launches per segment plus the per-AIR CPU overhead (`SymbolicConstraints::from`, DAG build, rule encode) for batched AIRs, without serializing extraction onto the critical path.\n\nCurrent: Round 0 = 179ms (90ms/seg). Expected after: Round 0 = 145-165ms (73-83ms/seg). Estimated net savings: 15-35ms on STARK excl trace (1106ms → 1071-1091ms).\n\nPrevious implementations (commits `0c699f47`, `bcb1c0d2`, `0d1bb2f9`) were reverted due to GPU OOM at APC 100/300. The OOM has since been resolved (VPMM 16 MiB page size + PRUNE_SHMEM_KERNELS), confirmed by the current APC 300 run at 1106ms.\n\n## Current Code Path\n\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n\n### Phase 1 (single-threaded, lines 1022-1198)\nBuilds `Vec<Round0AirWorkItem>` for all AIRs with proving key refs, trace pointers, pre-computed buffer sizes, eq_3bs, and `Round0ExtractTables`. Items sorted by descending height. Percentile buffer sizes computed for per-thread pre-allocation.\n\n### Phase 1.5 (overlapped background, lines 1341-1382)\nBackground thread uploads `d_eq_3b_per_trace` and precomputes `logup_combinations`, concurrent with Phase 2.\n\n### Phase 2 (multi-threaded, lines 1319-1413)\n8 OS threads, per-thread CUDA streams, round-robin assignment. Per AIR: `process_air_round0()` at `round0.rs` does:\n1. `evaluate_round0_zerocheck_gpu()` → zerocheck eval + reduction (~2 kernel launches)\n2. `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu()` → CPU rule construction (`SymbolicConstraints::from`, DAG, encode, H2D) + logup eval + reduction (~2 kernel launches)\n3. `_round0_extract_zerocheck_poly()` → GPU extraction to `d_batch_array` (1 kernel launch)\n4. `_round0_extract_logup_polys()` → GPU extraction to `d_batch_array` (1 kernel launch)\n\nAt APC 300: ~312 AIRs/seg, ~6 kernel launches/AIR = ~1872 launches/seg. Wall clock: ~90ms/seg.\n\n### Why it's slow at APC 300\nThe ~250 small AIRs (coset-parallel, height ≤ 256) each take ~0.2ms CPU work + ~0.1ms GPU eval + ~0.1ms extraction = ~0.4ms total. Across 8 threads: 31 per thread × 0.4ms ≈ 12ms. The remaining ~60 large AIRs take ~3-10ms each, ~8 per thread, total ~24-40ms. But measured per-segment Round 0 is ~90ms, with the difference attributable to CUDA driver overhead, stream scheduling, and memory pool contention across 1872 kernel launches.\n\n## Changes\n\n### Change 0: Diagnose the previous GPU hang\n\n**Before any code changes**, reproduce and diagnose the 12-minute GPU hang from commit `0d1bb2f9`:\n1. Cherry-pick `0d1bb2f9` onto a throwaway branch\n2. Build with debug symbols\n3. Run: `compute-sanitizer --tool memcheck -- $PROVE_BIN prove --artifact apc300.cbor --input 0 --recursion`\n4. If memcheck identifies an OOB access: note the location and fix in the new implementation\n5. If no memcheck error: the hang was likely caused by the OOM (now resolved) — this de-risks the approach\n6. Revert the cherry-pick\n\n### Change 1: Store logup Round 0 rules in proving key at keygen time\n\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/pkey.rs`\n\nAdd a `LogupRound0Rules` struct to `AirDataGpu` containing challenge-independent data only:\n- `d_rules: DeviceBuffer<u128>` — encoded DAG rules on GPU\n- `rules_len: usize` — number of rules\n- `buffer_size: u32` — logup intermediates buffer size (already present as `logup_round0_buffer_size`)\n- `dag_idx_to_rule_idx: Vec<usize>` — mapping from interaction index to rule index\n\n**NOT included** (challenge-dependent, computed per-proof):\n- Interaction weight vectors (`numer_weights`, `denom_weights`, `denom_sum_init`) — these depend on `beta_pows` and `eq_3bs` and must be computed at proving time\n\nThese rules are used **ONLY by the batch path** (Change 4). Phase 2's `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu` is unchanged and continues to reconstruct rules per-AIR, preserving the GPU pacing.\n\n### Change 2: CUDA Batched Kernels\n\n**Files:**\n- `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/zerocheck_round0.cu`\n- `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/logup_round0.cu`\n\nReplicate the descriptor-array kernel design from reverted commit `0d1bb2f9`:\n\n- **`batched_zerocheck_r0_coset_parallel_kernel`**: Block-to-AIR mapping via `Round0BlockCtx` array. Each `Round0ZcCtx` descriptor has per-AIR parameters (main/preprocessed pointers, constraint config, eq_xis, sels, intermediates offset, output offset). Only `GLOBAL=true, NEEDS_SHMEM=false` instantiation. Uses the existing single-AIR kernel body with a descriptor lookup preamble.\n\n- **`batched_logup_r0_coset_parallel_kernel`**: Same pattern with `Round0LogupCtx` descriptors. Uses keygen-time rules from Change 1 (device pointers in descriptor) plus proving-time interaction weights (computed in Change 4).\n\n- **`batched_final_reduce_block_sums`**: Reuse the existing reduction pattern from `batch_mle.cu`.\n\n**Null intermediates safety:** Descriptors for AIRs with `buffer_size == 0` get the arena base pointer as their intermediates pointer. The kernel guards intermediates writes with `if (buffer_size > 0)`. The `cudaErrorIllegalAddress` from commit `0c699f47` was caused by unconditional intermediates dereference; this guard prevents it.\n\n### Change 3: FFI Bindings\n\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs`\n\nAdd `#[repr(C)]` Rust structs:\n- `Round0BlockCtx { air_idx: u32, local_block_idx_x: u32 }`\n- `Round0ZcCtx` — main_trace_ptr, preprocessed_ptr, buffer_size, num_x, skip_domain, num_cosets, eq_xis_ptr, sels_ptr, intermediates_offset, output_offset\n- `Round0LogupCtx` — trace ptrs, d_rules_ptr, rules_len, d_numer_weights_ptr, d_denom_weights_ptr, buffer_size, d_eq_3b_ptr, intermediates_offset, output_offset\n\nAdd extern \"C\" declarations and safe Rust wrappers.\n\n### Change 4: Batch Orchestration Module\n\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0_batched.rs` (new file)\n\nAll public functions `#[inline(never)]`.\n\n**`identify_batchable_airs(work_items, l_skip) -> Vec<bool>`**\n- Batchable if: (a) coset-parallel (`num_x * skip_domain < 32768`), (b) intermediates within budget (`< 16M Fp` per AIR), (c) AIR has zerocheck constraints or logup interactions\n- Returns all-false if fewer than `MIN_BATCHABLE_AIRS = 50` qualify\n- **Also** computes and logs the aggregate intermediates size for the reviewer's L2 cache concern: `info!(\"Batch Round 0: {} AIRs, aggregate intermediates: {} MB\", count, total_bytes / 1_000_000)`\n\n**`batch_round0_eval_only(work_items, batch_mask, pk, d_batch_ptr, ...) -> Result<BatchEvalState>`**\nThis function runs on the default stream and performs **only the eval kernels**, NOT extraction. Returns a `BatchEvalState` containing per-AIR result pointers and metadata needed for extraction.\n\nSteps:\n1. Group batchable AIRs by `num_cosets_zc` (constraint_degree − 1)\n2. For each group:\n   a. Compute total intermediates size (sum of per-AIR `zc_intermed_cap + logup_intermed_cap`)\n   b. Allocate shared intermediates arena `DeviceBuffer`\n   c. Build `Round0ZcCtx` descriptors with arena offsets\n   d. Build `Round0BlockCtx` mapping\n   e. Upload descriptors to GPU\n   f. Launch `batched_zerocheck_r0_coset_parallel_kernel` + reduction\n   g. Compute proving-time interaction weights per AIR (CPU: ~10μs/AIR using `beta_pows` and `eq_3bs`)\n   h. Upload `d_numer_weights`, `d_denom_weights` to GPU\n   i. Build `Round0LogupCtx` descriptors using keygen-time rules from `pk.per_air[air_idx].other_data.logup_round0_rules`\n   j. Launch `batched_logup_r0_coset_parallel_kernel` + reduction\n3. Return `BatchEvalState` with per-AIR eval result offsets into the intermediates arena\n\n**Key design: extraction is NOT done here.** Extraction is deferred to Phase 2 worker threads (Change 5).\n\n### Change 5: Integration\n\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n\nInsert the batch eval between Phase 1 (after `current_stream_sync()` at line 1202) and the `num_threads` branch:\n\n```rust\n// Batch eval for small AIRs (default stream)\nlet batch_mask = round0_batched::identify_batchable_airs(&work_items, l_skip);\nlet batch_eval_state = if batch_mask.iter().any(|&b| b) {\n    let state = round0_batched::batch_round0_eval_only(\n        &work_items, &batch_mask, self.pk,\n        d_batch_array.as_mut_ptr(), l_skip,\n        &self.eq_3b_per_trace, &self.beta_pows,\n    )?;\n    current_stream_sync()?; // batch eval results visible to all streams\n    Some(state)\n} else {\n    None\n};\n```\n\nIn Phase 2 worker threads, handle batched AIRs with extraction-only:\n```rust\nfor &item_idx in &thread_items[thread_id] {\n    if batch_mask[item_idx] {\n        // Batch eval already done; only run extraction\n        let w = &work_items[item_idx];\n        round0_batched::extract_batched_air(\n            w, &batch_eval_state.as_ref().unwrap(),\n            batch_ptr_val as *mut EF, &extract_tables,\n        )?;\n    } else {\n        // Full per-AIR processing (eval + extraction, unchanged)\n        process_air_round0(&work_items[item_idx], &mut bufs, batch_ptr_val as *mut EF, &extract_tables)?;\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**Single-threaded path** (`num_threads <= 1`, lines 1280-1318): The batch path is skipped because `identify_batchable_airs` returns all-false (< 50 AIRs at APC 0). If somehow triggered, the single-threaded path would also check `batch_mask` — but this is a no-op since the mask is all-false.\n\n### Change 6: Visibility\n\nWiden `Round0AirWorkItem` and `Round0ExtractTables` to `pub(super)` and place `round0_batched.rs` as a submodule of `logup_zerocheck`.\n\n## Savings Breakdown (per segment at APC 300)\n\n| Component | Current | After | Change | Source |\n|-----------|---------|-------|--------|--------|\n| Batch eval (default stream) | 0ms | 5-8ms | +5-8ms | New: descriptor build + batched kernel |\n| Small AIR CPU work in Phase 2 | ~6ms/thread | 0ms | −6ms | Eliminated: skip SymbolicConstraints::from, rule build |\n| Small AIR eval launches in Phase 2 | ~5ms/thread | 0ms | −5ms | Eliminated: ~31 AIRs × 6 launches × 10μs |\n| Small AIR extraction in Phase 2 | ~3ms/thread | ~3ms/thread | 0ms | Unchanged: extraction runs on worker threads |\n| Large AIR processing in Phase 2 | ~40ms (max thread) | ~40ms (max thread) | 0ms | Unchanged |\n| CUDA overhead (scheduling, pool) | ~36ms | ~20-30ms | −6-16ms | Fewer kernel launches = less driver overhead |\n| **Total per segment** | **~90ms** | **~68-81ms** | **−9-22ms** | |\n| **Total (2 segments)** | **179ms** | **135-162ms** | **17-44ms** | |\n\nThe improvement is driven by: (1) eliminating ~11ms/thread of small-AIR CPU+launch overhead, and (2) reducing systemic CUDA driver overhead from fewer total kernel launches (~1872 → ~1372 per segment, a 27% reduction).\n\n## Invariants\n\n1. **Correctness**: Batched eval produces the same coset-parallel NTT + constraint evaluation as per-AIR eval. Extraction uses the identical per-AIR kernels and writes to the same `d_batch_array` offsets.\n\n2. **APC 0 guard**: `MIN_BATCHABLE_AIRS = 50` disables batching (APC 0 has ~20 AIRs/seg).\n\n3. **Phase 2 pacing preserved**: Phase 2 is unchanged for non-batched (large) AIRs. Per-AIR `SymbolicConstraints::from()` + rule building remain as GPU pacing for large AIRs.\n\n4. **Stream ordering**: Batch eval on default stream → `current_stream_sync()` → Phase 2 on per-thread streams. Batch eval results are visible before any extraction runs.\n\n5. **Extraction concurrency preserved**: Extraction for batched AIRs runs on Phase 2 worker threads (not the default stream), maintaining 8-way concurrent extraction just like the current code.\n\n6. **L2 cache budget**: The aggregate intermediates arena for ~250 small AIRs is logged at runtime. Expected size: 10-50MB (well within 72MB L2). If > 72MB, the L2 thrashing documented in `batch-global-gkr-input-eval` would apply and we'd see a regression — caught by measurement.\n\n7. **Null pointer safety**: Descriptors with `buffer_size == 0` get arena base pointer + kernel guards writes with `if (buffer_size > 0)`.\n\n## Measurement Plan\n\n1. **Step 0**: Run `compute-sanitizer --tool memcheck` on cherry-picked `0d1bb2f9` at APC 300\n2. Build: `cd /home/georg/powdr && cargo build --bin powdr_openvm_riscv -r --features \"metrics,cuda\"`\n3. APC 0: verify Round 0 ≤ 180ms, STARK excl trace ≤ 1810ms\n4. APC 300: expect Round 0 135-162ms (from 179ms), STARK excl trace 1062-1089ms\n5. APC 100 for completeness\n6. If Round 0 savings < 10ms: add tracing spans inside `batch_round0_eval_only` to identify bottleneck (descriptor build vs eval vs weight computation)\n\n## Rollback Criteria\n\n- **Hard revert**: APC 0 STARK excl trace regresses >20ms vs 1784ms\n- **Hard revert**: Verification failure at any APC config\n- **Hard revert**: GPU OOM, `cudaErrorIllegalAddress`, or GPU hang at any APC config\n- **Soft revert**: APC 300 Round 0 improvement <10ms\n- **Soft revert**: APC 300 STARK excl trace improvement <15ms\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":2,"oldLines":9,"newStart":2,"newLines":9,"lines":[" "," ## Goal"," ","-Reduce Round 0 wall-clock time at APC 300 by batching the ~250 small coset-parallel AIRs per segment. The batch path runs eval+extraction on the default CUDA stream before the multi-threaded Phase 2, which then only processes the remaining ~60 large AIRs. This eliminates ~500 eval kernel launches per segment and moves ~250 AIRs' CPU overhead (SymbolicConstraints::from, rule building) out of the multi-threaded critical path.","+Reduce Round 0 wall-clock time at APC 300 by batching the eval kernels for ~250 small coset-parallel AIRs per segment into 2-4 descriptor-array kernel launches on the default stream, then letting Phase 2 worker threads handle extraction for batched AIRs alongside full processing of the remaining ~60 large AIRs. This eliminates ~500 eval kernel launches per segment plus the per-AIR CPU overhead (`SymbolicConstraints::from`, DAG build, rule encode) for batched AIRs, without serializing extraction onto the critical path."," ","-Current: Round 0 = 179ms (90ms/seg). Expected after: Round 0 = 120-145ms (60-73ms/seg). Net savings: 35-60ms on STARK excl trace (1106ms → 1046-1071ms).","+Current: Round 0 = 179ms (90ms/seg). Expected after: Round 0 = 145-165ms (73-83ms/seg). Estimated net savings: 15-35ms on STARK excl trace (1106ms → 1071-1091ms)."," "," Previous implementations (commits `0c699f47`, `bcb1c0d2`, `0d1bb2f9`) were reverted due to GPU OOM at APC 100/300. The OOM has since been resolved (VPMM 16 MiB page size + PRUNE_SHMEM_KERNELS), confirmed by the current APC 300 run at 1106ms."," "]},{"oldStart":13,"oldLines":52,"newStart":13,"newLines":49,"lines":[" **File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`"," "," ### Phase 1 (single-threaded, lines 1022-1198)","-Builds `Vec<Round0AirWorkItem>` for all AIRs. Each work item has: proving key refs, trace pointers, pre-computed buffer sizes, eq_3bs, `Round0ExtractTables`. Items sorted by descending height. Percentile buffer sizes computed for pre-allocation.","+Builds `Vec<Round0AirWorkItem>` for all AIRs with proving key refs, trace pointers, pre-computed buffer sizes, eq_3bs, and `Round0ExtractTables`. Items sorted by descending height. Percentile buffer sizes computed for per-thread pre-allocation."," ","-### Phase 1.5 (overlapped background, lines 1341-1393)","+### Phase 1.5 (overlapped background, lines 1341-1382)"," Background thread uploads `d_eq_3b_per_trace` and precomputes `logup_combinations`, concurrent with Phase 2."," "," ### Phase 2 (multi-threaded, lines 1319-1413)","-8 OS threads, per-thread CUDA streams, round-robin assignment. Per AIR: `process_air_round0()` does:","-1. `evaluate_round0_zerocheck_gpu()` → zerocheck eval + reduction","-2. `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu()` → calls `SymbolicConstraints::from()`, builds DAG, encodes rules, H2D uploads, logup eval + reduction","-3. `_round0_extract_zerocheck_poly()` → GPU extraction to `d_batch_array`","-4. `_round0_extract_logup_polys()` → GPU extraction to `d_batch_array`","+8 OS threads, per-thread CUDA streams, round-robin assignment. Per AIR: `process_air_round0()` at `round0.rs` does:","+1. `evaluate_round0_zerocheck_gpu()` → zerocheck eval + reduction (~2 kernel launches)","+2. `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu()` → CPU rule construction (`SymbolicConstraints::from`, DAG, encode, H2D) + logup eval + reduction (~2 kernel launches)","+3. `_round0_extract_zerocheck_poly()` → GPU extraction to `d_batch_array` (1 kernel launch)","+4. `_round0_extract_logup_polys()` → GPU extraction to `d_batch_array` (1 kernel launch)"," ","-At APC 300: ~312 AIRs/seg, ~4 kernel launches/AIR = ~1248 eval+extraction launches/seg. Wall clock: ~90ms/seg.","+At APC 300: ~312 AIRs/seg, ~6 kernel launches/AIR = ~1872 launches/seg. Wall clock: ~90ms/seg."," "," ### Why it's slow at APC 300","-Phase 2 processes ~312 AIRs across 8 threads (~39/thread). For the ~250 small AIRs (height ≤ 256), each one has:","-- CPU cost: `SymbolicConstraints::from()` (~0.1ms) + DAG build + rule encode in `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu()` (~0.1ms)","-- GPU eval time: ~50-200μs (tiny, GPU-underutilized)","-- 4 kernel launches with ~10μs overhead each","+The ~250 small AIRs (coset-parallel, height ≤ 256) each take ~0.2ms CPU work + ~0.1ms GPU eval + ~0.1ms extraction = ~0.4ms total. Across 8 threads: 31 per thread × 0.4ms ≈ 12ms. The remaining ~60 large AIRs take ~3-10ms each, ~8 per thread, total ~24-40ms. But measured per-segment Round 0 is ~90ms, with the difference attributable to CUDA driver overhead, stream scheduling, and memory pool contention across 1872 kernel launches."," ","-The per-AIR CPU work (~0.2ms) dominates over GPU compute for small AIRs. 250 small AIRs × 0.2ms / 8 threads ≈ 6ms of serialized CPU overhead per thread. The GPU eval of these small AIRs takes ~4ms/thread but is interleaved with large AIRs.","-"," ## Changes"," "," ### Change 0: Diagnose the previous GPU hang"," ","-**Before any code changes**, run the reverted batch Round 0 kernels from commit `0d1bb2f9` under `compute-sanitizer --tool memcheck` to identify whether the 12-minute hang at APC 300 (reported in the 1600 report) was caused by an out-of-bounds memory access, infinite loop, or other bug. Steps:","+**Before any code changes**, reproduce and diagnose the 12-minute GPU hang from commit `0d1bb2f9`:"," 1. Cherry-pick `0d1bb2f9` onto a throwaway branch"," 2. Build with debug symbols"," 3. Run: `compute-sanitizer --tool memcheck -- $PROVE_BIN prove --artifact apc300.cbor --input 0 --recursion`","-4. If memcheck identifies an OOB access: fix the specific bug in the new implementation","-5. If memcheck shows no errors: the hang was likely caused by the OOM (now resolved) or by the Rust optimizer issue (fixed by `#[inline(never)]`)","-6. Revert the cherry-pick before proceeding","+4. If memcheck identifies an OOB access: note the location and fix in the new implementation","+5. If no memcheck error: the hang was likely caused by the OOM (now resolved) — this de-risks the approach","+6. Revert the cherry-pick"," ","-This step de-risks the CUDA kernel code before investing in the Rust orchestration.","-"," ### Change 1: Store logup Round 0 rules in proving key at keygen time"," ","-**Files:**","-- `crates/cuda-backend/src/pkey.rs`","+**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/pkey.rs`"," ","-Add a `LogupRound0Rules` struct to `AirDataGpu` containing the encoded logup DAG rules + interaction-to-rule-index mapping + per-challenge weight vectors. This is the same keygen-time pre-computation from commit `5bec2ee1` (reverted `52873be4`), but the stored rules are used **ONLY by the batch path** (Change 3), NOT by Phase 2. Phase 2 continues to reconstruct rules per-AIR as before, preserving the beneficial GPU pacing.","+Add a `LogupRound0Rules` struct to `AirDataGpu` containing challenge-independent data only:","+- `d_rules: DeviceBuffer<u128>` — encoded DAG rules on GPU","+- `rules_len: usize` — number of rules","+- `buffer_size: u32` — logup intermediates buffer size (already present as `logup_round0_buffer_size`)","+- `dag_idx_to_rule_idx: Vec<usize>` — mapping from interaction index to rule index"," ","-The `logup_round0_buffer_size` field is already present in `AirDataGpu` (added by the `prealloc-round0-threshold-buffers` task). This change adds the full rules alongside it.","+**NOT included** (challenge-dependent, computed per-proof):","+- Interaction weight vectors (`numer_weights`, `denom_weights`, `denom_sum_init`) — these depend on `beta_pows` and `eq_3bs` and must be computed at proving time"," ","-**Why this doesn't regress like commit 5bec2ee1:** That commit modified Phase 2's `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu` to use keygen-time rules, removing the per-AIR CPU work that served as GPU pacing. This change does NOT modify Phase 2 at all — Phase 2 is unchanged. The keygen rules are only consumed by the new `batch_round0_small_airs` function (Change 3).","+These rules are used **ONLY by the batch path** (Change 4). Phase 2's `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu` is unchanged and continues to reconstruct rules per-AIR, preserving the GPU pacing."," "," ### Change 2: CUDA Batched Kernels"," "]},{"oldStart":68,"oldLines":109,"newStart":65,"newLines":140,"lines":[" "," Replicate the descriptor-array kernel design from reverted commit `0d1bb2f9`:"," ","-- **`batched_zerocheck_r0_coset_parallel_kernel`**: Block-to-AIR mapping via `Round0BlockCtx` array. Each `Round0ZcCtx` descriptor has all per-AIR parameters. Only `GLOBAL=true, NEEDS_SHMEM=false` instantiation (PRUNE_SHMEM_KERNELS active). Uses the existing single-AIR kernel body, wrapped with a descriptor lookup preamble.","+- **`batched_zerocheck_r0_coset_parallel_kernel`**: Block-to-AIR mapping via `Round0BlockCtx` array. Each `Round0ZcCtx` descriptor has per-AIR parameters (main/preprocessed pointers, constraint config, eq_xis, sels, intermediates offset, output offset). Only `GLOBAL=true, NEEDS_SHMEM=false` instantiation. Uses the existing single-AIR kernel body with a descriptor lookup preamble."," ","-- **`batched_logup_r0_coset_parallel_kernel`**: Same pattern with `Round0LogupCtx` descriptors. Uses keygen-time pre-computed rules (device pointers from Change 1).","+- **`batched_logup_r0_coset_parallel_kernel`**: Same pattern with `Round0LogupCtx` descriptors. Uses keygen-time rules from Change 1 (device pointers in descriptor) plus proving-time interaction weights (computed in Change 4)."," "," - **`batched_final_reduce_block_sums`**: Reuse the existing reduction pattern from `batch_mle.cu`."," ","-**Null intermediates:** For AIRs with `zc_intermed_cap == 0` (no zerocheck constraints) or `logup_intermed_cap == 0`, the descriptor's intermediates pointer is set to a valid offset in the arena (pointing past all used data). The kernel code already guards against `buffer_size == 0` by skipping the intermediates write path. The previous `cudaErrorIllegalAddress` (from commit `0c699f47`) occurred because GLOBAL-mode kernels unconditionally dereferenced intermediates for all blocks — the batched kernel must check `buffer_size > 0` before writing to intermediates, or the null descriptor must be excluded from the launch.","+**Null intermediates safety:** Descriptors for AIRs with `buffer_size == 0` get the arena base pointer as their intermediates pointer. The kernel guards intermediates writes with `if (buffer_size > 0)`. The `cudaErrorIllegalAddress` from commit `0c699f47` was caused by unconditional intermediates dereference; this guard prevents it."," "," ### Change 3: FFI Bindings"," "," **File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs`"," ","-Add `#[repr(C)]` Rust structs mirroring the CUDA descriptors:","+Add `#[repr(C)]` Rust structs:"," - `Round0BlockCtx { air_idx: u32, local_block_idx_x: u32 }`","-- `Round0ZcCtx` with fields: main_trace_ptr, preprocessed_ptr, buffer_size, num_x, skip_domain, num_cosets, eq_xis_ptr, sels_ptr, output_ptr, output_offset","-- `Round0LogupCtx` with fields: trace ptrs, encoded_rules_ptr, rules_len, weight ptrs, buffer_size, eq_3b_ptr, output_ptr, output_offset","+- `Round0ZcCtx` — main_trace_ptr, preprocessed_ptr, buffer_size, num_x, skip_domain, num_cosets, eq_xis_ptr, sels_ptr, intermediates_offset, output_offset","+- `Round0LogupCtx` — trace ptrs, d_rules_ptr, rules_len, d_numer_weights_ptr, d_denom_weights_ptr, buffer_size, d_eq_3b_ptr, intermediates_offset, output_offset"," ","-Add extern \"C\" declarations and safe wrappers.","+Add extern \"C\" declarations and safe Rust wrappers."," "," ### Change 4: Batch Orchestration Module"," "," **File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0_batched.rs` (new file)"," ","-All public functions `#[inline(never)]` to prevent Rust optimizer interference.","+All public functions `#[inline(never)]`."," "," **`identify_batchable_airs(work_items, l_skip) -> Vec<bool>`**","-- Batchable if: (a) coset-parallel (`num_x * skip_domain < 32768`), (b) intermediates within budget (`< 16M Fp`), (c) AIR has zerocheck OR logup work","-- Returns all-false if fewer than 50 qualify (disabled at APC 0 with ~20 AIRs/seg)","+- Batchable if: (a) coset-parallel (`num_x * skip_domain < 32768`), (b) intermediates within budget (`< 16M Fp` per AIR), (c) AIR has zerocheck constraints or logup interactions","+- Returns all-false if fewer than `MIN_BATCHABLE_AIRS = 50` qualify","+- **Also** computes and logs the aggregate intermediates size for the reviewer's L2 cache concern: `info!(\"Batch Round 0: {} AIRs, aggregate intermediates: {} MB\", count, total_bytes / 1_000_000)`"," ","-**`batch_round0_small_airs(work_items, batch_mask, pk, extract_tables, d_batch_ptr, ...) -> Result<()>`**","-1. Group batchable AIRs by `num_cosets_zc` (constraint_degree − 1) — AIRs with different num_cosets need separate launches.","+**`batch_round0_eval_only(work_items, batch_mask, pk, d_batch_ptr, ...) -> Result<BatchEvalState>`**","+This function runs on the default stream and performs **only the eval kernels**, NOT extraction. Returns a `BatchEvalState` containing per-AIR result pointers and metadata needed for extraction.","+","+Steps:","+1. Group batchable AIRs by `num_cosets_zc` (constraint_degree − 1)"," 2. For each group:","-   a. Compute total intermediates size (sum of per-AIR sizes) and allocate shared arena `DeviceBuffer`","-   b. Build `Round0ZcCtx` descriptors: use proving key pointers (trace, preprocessed, zerocheck config) and arena offsets for intermediates. Output offsets point into `d_batch_array` at each AIR's `trace_idx`.","-   c. Build `Round0BlockCtx` mapping array","-   d. Upload descriptors + block_ctxs to GPU","-   e. Launch `batched_zerocheck_r0_coset_parallel_kernel` + reduction","-   f. Build `Round0LogupCtx` descriptors: use keygen-time logup rules from `pk.per_air[air_idx].other_data.logup_round0_rules` (Change 1). Compute per-challenge interaction weights from current `beta_pows` and `eq_3bs`.","-   g. Launch `batched_logup_r0_coset_parallel_kernel` + reduction","-   h. For each batched AIR: call `_round0_extract_zerocheck_poly()` and `_round0_extract_logup_polys()` to write final polynomial coefficients into `d_batch_array`","-3. Sync default stream","+   a. Compute total intermediates size (sum of per-AIR `zc_intermed_cap + logup_intermed_cap`)","+   b. Allocate shared intermediates arena `DeviceBuffer`","+   c. Build `Round0ZcCtx` descriptors with arena offsets","+   d. Build `Round0BlockCtx` mapping","+   e. Upload descriptors to GPU","+   f. Launch `batched_zerocheck_r0_coset_parallel_kernel` + reduction","+   g. Compute proving-time interaction weights per AIR (CPU: ~10μs/AIR using `beta_pows` and `eq_3bs`)","+   h. Upload `d_numer_weights`, `d_denom_weights` to GPU","+   i. Build `Round0LogupCtx` descriptors using keygen-time rules from `pk.per_air[air_idx].other_data.logup_round0_rules`","+   j. Launch `batched_logup_r0_coset_parallel_kernel` + reduction","+3. Return `BatchEvalState` with per-AIR eval result offsets into the intermediates arena"," ","-**Per-AIR extraction (step 2h):** The ~500 extraction launches (250 AIRs × 2) add ~25ms on the default stream. This is the largest cost in the batch path. A future iteration could batch extraction too, but per-AIR extraction is simpler, uses the proven existing kernels, and keeps this change more manageable.","+**Key design: extraction is NOT done here.** Extraction is deferred to Phase 2 worker threads (Change 5)."," ","-**Per-AIR interaction weight computation (step 2f):** Computing interaction weights requires current `beta_pows` and `eq_3bs` values (challenge-dependent, can't be pre-computed at keygen). This is ~10μs per AIR of CPU arithmetic. For 250 AIRs: 2.5ms. Not a significant cost.","-"," ### Change 5: Integration"," "," **File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`"," ","-Insert the batch path between Phase 1 and the `num_threads` branching point (line 1208). The batch path runs only in the multi-threaded case (`num_threads > 1`, i.e., APC 100/300 with ≥100 AIRs). In the single-threaded case (`num_threads <= 1`, APC 0), the batch path is skipped because `identify_batchable_airs` returns all-false (< 50 qualifying AIRs).","+Insert the batch eval between Phase 1 (after `current_stream_sync()` at line 1202) and the `num_threads` branch:"," "," ```rust","-// After Phase 1 (work items + extract tables built, d_batch_array allocated, sync done)","+// Batch eval for small AIRs (default stream)"," let batch_mask = round0_batched::identify_batchable_airs(&work_items, l_skip);","-let has_batched = batch_mask.iter().any(|&b| b);","-if has_batched {","-    round0_batched::batch_round0_small_airs(","-        &work_items, &batch_mask, self.pk, &extract_tables,","+let batch_eval_state = if batch_mask.iter().any(|&b| b) {","+    let state = round0_batched::batch_round0_eval_only(","+        &work_items, &batch_mask, self.pk,","         d_batch_array.as_mut_ptr(), l_skip,","         &self.eq_3b_per_trace, &self.beta_pows,","     )?;","-    // batch writes to d_batch_array on default stream; sync before worker threads start","-    current_stream_sync()?;","-}","+    current_stream_sync()?; // batch eval results visible to all streams","+    Some(state)","+} else {","+    None","+};"," ```"," ","-In Phase 2, the worker threads skip batched AIRs:","+In Phase 2 worker threads, handle batched AIRs with extraction-only:"," ```rust"," for &item_idx in &thread_items[thread_id] {","-    if batch_mask[item_idx] { continue; }","-    process_air_round0(&work_items[item_idx], &mut bufs, batch_ptr_val as *mut EF, &extract_tables)?;","+    if batch_mask[item_idx] {","+        // Batch eval already done; only run extraction","+        let w = &work_items[item_idx];","+        round0_batched::extract_batched_air(","+            w, &batch_eval_state.as_ref().unwrap(),","+            batch_ptr_val as *mut EF, &extract_tables,","+        )?;","+    } else {","+        // Full per-AIR processing (eval + extraction, unchanged)","+        process_air_round0(&work_items[item_idx], &mut bufs, batch_ptr_val as *mut EF, &extract_tables)?;","+    }"," }"," ```"," ","+**Single-threaded path** (`num_threads <= 1`, lines 1280-1318): The batch path is skipped because `identify_batchable_airs` returns all-false (< 50 AIRs at APC 0). If somehow triggered, the single-threaded path would also check `batch_mask` — but this is a no-op since the mask is all-false.","+"," ### Change 6: Visibility"," ","-**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`","+Widen `Round0AirWorkItem` and `Round0ExtractTables` to `pub(super)` and place `round0_batched.rs` as a submodule of `logup_zerocheck`."," ","-Widen `Round0AirWorkItem` and `Round0ExtractTables` to `pub(super)` or place `round0_batched.rs` as a submodule of `logup_zerocheck` so it has access.","+## Savings Breakdown (per segment at APC 300)"," ","+| Component | Current | After | Change | Source |","+|-----------|---------|-------|--------|--------|","+| Batch eval (default stream) | 0ms | 5-8ms | +5-8ms | New: descriptor build + batched kernel |","+| Small AIR CPU work in Phase 2 | ~6ms/thread | 0ms | −6ms | Eliminated: skip SymbolicConstraints::from, rule build |","+| Small AIR eval launches in Phase 2 | ~5ms/thread | 0ms | −5ms | Eliminated: ~31 AIRs × 6 launches × 10μs |","+| Small AIR extraction in Phase 2 | ~3ms/thread | ~3ms/thread | 0ms | Unchanged: extraction runs on worker threads |","+| Large AIR processing in Phase 2 | ~40ms (max thread) | ~40ms (max thread) | 0ms | Unchanged |","+| CUDA overhead (scheduling, pool) | ~36ms | ~20-30ms | −6-16ms | Fewer kernel launches = less driver overhead |","+| **Total per segment** | **~90ms** | **~68-81ms** | **−9-22ms** | |","+| **Total (2 segments)** | **179ms** | **135-162ms** | **17-44ms** | |","+","+The improvement is driven by: (1) eliminating ~11ms/thread of small-AIR CPU+launch overhead, and (2) reducing systemic CUDA driver overhead from fewer total kernel launches (~1872 → ~1372 per segment, a 27% reduction).","+"," ## Invariants"," ","-1. **Correctness**: Batched eval produces the same coset-parallel NTT + constraint evaluation as per-AIR eval. Extraction uses the identical per-AIR kernels, writing to the same `d_batch_array` offsets.","+1. **Correctness**: Batched eval produces the same coset-parallel NTT + constraint evaluation as per-AIR eval. Extraction uses the identical per-AIR kernels and writes to the same `d_batch_array` offsets."," ","-2. **APC 0 guard**: `MIN_BATCHABLE_AIRS = 50` disables batching at APC 0 (≤20 AIRs/seg). The single-threaded path (`num_threads <= 1`) is completely unchanged.","+2. **APC 0 guard**: `MIN_BATCHABLE_AIRS = 50` disables batching (APC 0 has ~20 AIRs/seg)."," ","-3. **Phase 2 pacing preserved**: Phase 2's `process_air_round0` is unchanged for non-batched AIRs. The per-AIR `SymbolicConstraints::from()` + rule building remains as GPU pacing for large AIRs. Phase 2 does NOT use the keygen-time logup rules.","+3. **Phase 2 pacing preserved**: Phase 2 is unchanged for non-batched (large) AIRs. Per-AIR `SymbolicConstraints::from()` + rule building remain as GPU pacing for large AIRs."," ","-4. **Stream ordering**: Batch path on default stream → `current_stream_sync()` → Phase 2 on per-thread streams. Batch results visible to all worker threads. Phase 2 results joined at scope exit.","+4. **Stream ordering**: Batch eval on default stream → `current_stream_sync()` → Phase 2 on per-thread streams. Batch eval results are visible before any extraction runs."," ","-5. **Memory**: Shared intermediates arena sized by summing per-AIR needs. Typical size: 10-50MB for ~250 small AIRs (well within L2 cache). Per-AIR budget cap (16M Fp ≈ 64MB) prevents outliers from inflating the arena.","+5. **Extraction concurrency preserved**: Extraction for batched AIRs runs on Phase 2 worker threads (not the default stream), maintaining 8-way concurrent extraction just like the current code."," ","-6. **Null pointer safety**: Descriptors for AIRs with `buffer_size == 0` (no intermediates needed) get the arena base pointer as intermediates. The kernel checks `buffer_size > 0` before writing to intermediates. This avoids the `cudaErrorIllegalAddress` from the original attempt.","+6. **L2 cache budget**: The aggregate intermediates arena for ~250 small AIRs is logged at runtime. Expected size: 10-50MB (well within 72MB L2). If > 72MB, the L2 thrashing documented in `batch-global-gkr-input-eval` would apply and we'd see a regression — caught by measurement."," ","+7. **Null pointer safety**: Descriptors with `buffer_size == 0` get arena base pointer + kernel guards writes with `if (buffer_size > 0)`.","+"," ## Measurement Plan"," ","-1. **Step 0**: Run `compute-sanitizer --tool memcheck` on cherry-picked `0d1bb2f9` to diagnose the previous GPU hang (see Change 0)","+1. **Step 0**: Run `compute-sanitizer --tool memcheck` on cherry-picked `0d1bb2f9` at APC 300"," 2. Build: `cd /home/georg/powdr && cargo build --bin powdr_openvm_riscv -r --features \"metrics,cuda\"`","-3. APC 0 regression: verify Round 0 ≤ 180ms, STARK excl trace ≤ 1810ms","-4. APC 300: expect Round 0 120-145ms (from 179ms), STARK excl trace 1046-1071ms","+3. APC 0: verify Round 0 ≤ 180ms, STARK excl trace ≤ 1810ms","+4. APC 300: expect Round 0 135-162ms (from 179ms), STARK excl trace 1062-1089ms"," 5. APC 100 for completeness","-6. If APC 300 passes but Round 0 savings < 25ms: profile batch path overhead with tracing spans to identify whether descriptor building, extraction, or eval dominates","+6. If Round 0 savings < 10ms: add tracing spans inside `batch_round0_eval_only` to identify bottleneck (descriptor build vs eval vs weight computation)"," "," ## Rollback Criteria"," "]},{"oldStart":178,"oldLines":4,"newStart":206,"newLines":4,"lines":[" - **Hard revert**: Verification failure at any APC config"," - **Hard revert**: GPU OOM, `cudaErrorIllegalAddress`, or GPU hang at any APC config"," - **Soft revert**: APC 300 Round 0 improvement <10ms","-- **Soft revert**: APC 300 STARK excl trace improvement <20ms","+- **Soft revert**: APC 300 STARK excl trace improvement <15ms"]}],"originalFile":"# Plan: Re-enable Batch Round 0 Descriptor-Array Kernels for Small AIRs\n\n## Goal\n\nReduce Round 0 wall-clock time at APC 300 by batching the ~250 small coset-parallel AIRs per segment. The batch path runs eval+extraction on the default CUDA stream before the multi-threaded Phase 2, which then only processes the remaining ~60 large AIRs. This eliminates ~500 eval kernel launches per segment and moves ~250 AIRs' CPU overhead (SymbolicConstraints::from, rule building) out of the multi-threaded critical path.\n\nCurrent: Round 0 = 179ms (90ms/seg). Expected after: Round 0 = 120-145ms (60-73ms/seg). Net savings: 35-60ms on STARK excl trace (1106ms → 1046-1071ms).\n\nPrevious implementations (commits `0c699f47`, `bcb1c0d2`, `0d1bb2f9`) were reverted due to GPU OOM at APC 100/300. The OOM has since been resolved (VPMM 16 MiB page size + PRUNE_SHMEM_KERNELS), confirmed by the current APC 300 run at 1106ms.\n\n## Current Code Path\n\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n\n### Phase 1 (single-threaded, lines 1022-1198)\nBuilds `Vec<Round0AirWorkItem>` for all AIRs. Each work item has: proving key refs, trace pointers, pre-computed buffer sizes, eq_3bs, `Round0ExtractTables`. Items sorted by descending height. Percentile buffer sizes computed for pre-allocation.\n\n### Phase 1.5 (overlapped background, lines 1341-1393)\nBackground thread uploads `d_eq_3b_per_trace` and precomputes `logup_combinations`, concurrent with Phase 2.\n\n### Phase 2 (multi-threaded, lines 1319-1413)\n8 OS threads, per-thread CUDA streams, round-robin assignment. Per AIR: `process_air_round0()` does:\n1. `evaluate_round0_zerocheck_gpu()` → zerocheck eval + reduction\n2. `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu()` → calls `SymbolicConstraints::from()`, builds DAG, encodes rules, H2D uploads, logup eval + reduction\n3. `_round0_extract_zerocheck_poly()` → GPU extraction to `d_batch_array`\n4. `_round0_extract_logup_polys()` → GPU extraction to `d_batch_array`\n\nAt APC 300: ~312 AIRs/seg, ~4 kernel launches/AIR = ~1248 eval+extraction launches/seg. Wall clock: ~90ms/seg.\n\n### Why it's slow at APC 300\nPhase 2 processes ~312 AIRs across 8 threads (~39/thread). For the ~250 small AIRs (height ≤ 256), each one has:\n- CPU cost: `SymbolicConstraints::from()` (~0.1ms) + DAG build + rule encode in `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu()` (~0.1ms)\n- GPU eval time: ~50-200μs (tiny, GPU-underutilized)\n- 4 kernel launches with ~10μs overhead each\n\nThe per-AIR CPU work (~0.2ms) dominates over GPU compute for small AIRs. 250 small AIRs × 0.2ms / 8 threads ≈ 6ms of serialized CPU overhead per thread. The GPU eval of these small AIRs takes ~4ms/thread but is interleaved with large AIRs.\n\n## Changes\n\n### Change 0: Diagnose the previous GPU hang\n\n**Before any code changes**, run the reverted batch Round 0 kernels from commit `0d1bb2f9` under `compute-sanitizer --tool memcheck` to identify whether the 12-minute hang at APC 300 (reported in the 1600 report) was caused by an out-of-bounds memory access, infinite loop, or other bug. Steps:\n1. Cherry-pick `0d1bb2f9` onto a throwaway branch\n2. Build with debug symbols\n3. Run: `compute-sanitizer --tool memcheck -- $PROVE_BIN prove --artifact apc300.cbor --input 0 --recursion`\n4. If memcheck identifies an OOB access: fix the specific bug in the new implementation\n5. If memcheck shows no errors: the hang was likely caused by the OOM (now resolved) or by the Rust optimizer issue (fixed by `#[inline(never)]`)\n6. Revert the cherry-pick before proceeding\n\nThis step de-risks the CUDA kernel code before investing in the Rust orchestration.\n\n### Change 1: Store logup Round 0 rules in proving key at keygen time\n\n**Files:**\n- `crates/cuda-backend/src/pkey.rs`\n\nAdd a `LogupRound0Rules` struct to `AirDataGpu` containing the encoded logup DAG rules + interaction-to-rule-index mapping + per-challenge weight vectors. This is the same keygen-time pre-computation from commit `5bec2ee1` (reverted `52873be4`), but the stored rules are used **ONLY by the batch path** (Change 3), NOT by Phase 2. Phase 2 continues to reconstruct rules per-AIR as before, preserving the beneficial GPU pacing.\n\nThe `logup_round0_buffer_size` field is already present in `AirDataGpu` (added by the `prealloc-round0-threshold-buffers` task). This change adds the full rules alongside it.\n\n**Why this doesn't regress like commit 5bec2ee1:** That commit modified Phase 2's `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu` to use keygen-time rules, removing the per-AIR CPU work that served as GPU pacing. This change does NOT modify Phase 2 at all — Phase 2 is unchanged. The keygen rules are only consumed by the new `batch_round0_small_airs` function (Change 3).\n\n### Change 2: CUDA Batched Kernels\n\n**Files:**\n- `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/zerocheck_round0.cu`\n- `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/logup_round0.cu`\n\nReplicate the descriptor-array kernel design from reverted commit `0d1bb2f9`:\n\n- **`batched_zerocheck_r0_coset_parallel_kernel`**: Block-to-AIR mapping via `Round0BlockCtx` array. Each `Round0ZcCtx` descriptor has all per-AIR parameters. Only `GLOBAL=true, NEEDS_SHMEM=false` instantiation (PRUNE_SHMEM_KERNELS active). Uses the existing single-AIR kernel body, wrapped with a descriptor lookup preamble.\n\n- **`batched_logup_r0_coset_parallel_kernel`**: Same pattern with `Round0LogupCtx` descriptors. Uses keygen-time pre-computed rules (device pointers from Change 1).\n\n- **`batched_final_reduce_block_sums`**: Reuse the existing reduction pattern from `batch_mle.cu`.\n\n**Null intermediates:** For AIRs with `zc_intermed_cap == 0` (no zerocheck constraints) or `logup_intermed_cap == 0`, the descriptor's intermediates pointer is set to a valid offset in the arena (pointing past all used data). The kernel code already guards against `buffer_size == 0` by skipping the intermediates write path. The previous `cudaErrorIllegalAddress` (from commit `0c699f47`) occurred because GLOBAL-mode kernels unconditionally dereferenced intermediates for all blocks — the batched kernel must check `buffer_size > 0` before writing to intermediates, or the null descriptor must be excluded from the launch.\n\n### Change 3: FFI Bindings\n\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs`\n\nAdd `#[repr(C)]` Rust structs mirroring the CUDA descriptors:\n- `Round0BlockCtx { air_idx: u32, local_block_idx_x: u32 }`\n- `Round0ZcCtx` with fields: main_trace_ptr, preprocessed_ptr, buffer_size, num_x, skip_domain, num_cosets, eq_xis_ptr, sels_ptr, output_ptr, output_offset\n- `Round0LogupCtx` with fields: trace ptrs, encoded_rules_ptr, rules_len, weight ptrs, buffer_size, eq_3b_ptr, output_ptr, output_offset\n\nAdd extern \"C\" declarations and safe wrappers.\n\n### Change 4: Batch Orchestration Module\n\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0_batched.rs` (new file)\n\nAll public functions `#[inline(never)]` to prevent Rust optimizer interference.\n\n**`identify_batchable_airs(work_items, l_skip) -> Vec<bool>`**\n- Batchable if: (a) coset-parallel (`num_x * skip_domain < 32768`), (b) intermediates within budget (`< 16M Fp`), (c) AIR has zerocheck OR logup work\n- Returns all-false if fewer than 50 qualify (disabled at APC 0 with ~20 AIRs/seg)\n\n**`batch_round0_small_airs(work_items, batch_mask, pk, extract_tables, d_batch_ptr, ...) -> Result<()>`**\n1. Group batchable AIRs by `num_cosets_zc` (constraint_degree − 1) — AIRs with different num_cosets need separate launches.\n2. For each group:\n   a. Compute total intermediates size (sum of per-AIR sizes) and allocate shared arena `DeviceBuffer`\n   b. Build `Round0ZcCtx` descriptors: use proving key pointers (trace, preprocessed, zerocheck config) and arena offsets for intermediates. Output offsets point into `d_batch_array` at each AIR's `trace_idx`.\n   c. Build `Round0BlockCtx` mapping array\n   d. Upload descriptors + block_ctxs to GPU\n   e. Launch `batched_zerocheck_r0_coset_parallel_kernel` + reduction\n   f. Build `Round0LogupCtx` descriptors: use keygen-time logup rules from `pk.per_air[air_idx].other_data.logup_round0_rules` (Change 1). Compute per-challenge interaction weights from current `beta_pows` and `eq_3bs`.\n   g. Launch `batched_logup_r0_coset_parallel_kernel` + reduction\n   h. For each batched AIR: call `_round0_extract_zerocheck_poly()` and `_round0_extract_logup_polys()` to write final polynomial coefficients into `d_batch_array`\n3. Sync default stream\n\n**Per-AIR extraction (step 2h):** The ~500 extraction launches (250 AIRs × 2) add ~25ms on the default stream. This is the largest cost in the batch path. A future iteration could batch extraction too, but per-AIR extraction is simpler, uses the proven existing kernels, and keeps this change more manageable.\n\n**Per-AIR interaction weight computation (step 2f):** Computing interaction weights requires current `beta_pows` and `eq_3bs` values (challenge-dependent, can't be pre-computed at keygen). This is ~10μs per AIR of CPU arithmetic. For 250 AIRs: 2.5ms. Not a significant cost.\n\n### Change 5: Integration\n\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n\nInsert the batch path between Phase 1 and the `num_threads` branching point (line 1208). The batch path runs only in the multi-threaded case (`num_threads > 1`, i.e., APC 100/300 with ≥100 AIRs). In the single-threaded case (`num_threads <= 1`, APC 0), the batch path is skipped because `identify_batchable_airs` returns all-false (< 50 qualifying AIRs).\n\n```rust\n// After Phase 1 (work items + extract tables built, d_batch_array allocated, sync done)\nlet batch_mask = round0_batched::identify_batchable_airs(&work_items, l_skip);\nlet has_batched = batch_mask.iter().any(|&b| b);\nif has_batched {\n    round0_batched::batch_round0_small_airs(\n        &work_items, &batch_mask, self.pk, &extract_tables,\n        d_batch_array.as_mut_ptr(), l_skip,\n        &self.eq_3b_per_trace, &self.beta_pows,\n    )?;\n    // batch writes to d_batch_array on default stream; sync before worker threads start\n    current_stream_sync()?;\n}\n```\n\nIn Phase 2, the worker threads skip batched AIRs:\n```rust\nfor &item_idx in &thread_items[thread_id] {\n    if batch_mask[item_idx] { continue; }\n    process_air_round0(&work_items[item_idx], &mut bufs, batch_ptr_val as *mut EF, &extract_tables)?;\n}\n```\n\n### Change 6: Visibility\n\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n\nWiden `Round0AirWorkItem` and `Round0ExtractTables` to `pub(super)` or place `round0_batched.rs` as a submodule of `logup_zerocheck` so it has access.\n\n## Invariants\n\n1. **Correctness**: Batched eval produces the same coset-parallel NTT + constraint evaluation as per-AIR eval. Extraction uses the identical per-AIR kernels, writing to the same `d_batch_array` offsets.\n\n2. **APC 0 guard**: `MIN_BATCHABLE_AIRS = 50` disables batching at APC 0 (≤20 AIRs/seg). The single-threaded path (`num_threads <= 1`) is completely unchanged.\n\n3. **Phase 2 pacing preserved**: Phase 2's `process_air_round0` is unchanged for non-batched AIRs. The per-AIR `SymbolicConstraints::from()` + rule building remains as GPU pacing for large AIRs. Phase 2 does NOT use the keygen-time logup rules.\n\n4. **Stream ordering**: Batch path on default stream → `current_stream_sync()` → Phase 2 on per-thread streams. Batch results visible to all worker threads. Phase 2 results joined at scope exit.\n\n5. **Memory**: Shared intermediates arena sized by summing per-AIR needs. Typical size: 10-50MB for ~250 small AIRs (well within L2 cache). Per-AIR budget cap (16M Fp ≈ 64MB) prevents outliers from inflating the arena.\n\n6. **Null pointer safety**: Descriptors for AIRs with `buffer_size == 0` (no intermediates needed) get the arena base pointer as intermediates. The kernel checks `buffer_size > 0` before writing to intermediates. This avoids the `cudaErrorIllegalAddress` from the original attempt.\n\n## Measurement Plan\n\n1. **Step 0**: Run `compute-sanitizer --tool memcheck` on cherry-picked `0d1bb2f9` to diagnose the previous GPU hang (see Change 0)\n2. Build: `cd /home/georg/powdr && cargo build --bin powdr_openvm_riscv -r --features \"metrics,cuda\"`\n3. APC 0 regression: verify Round 0 ≤ 180ms, STARK excl trace ≤ 1810ms\n4. APC 300: expect Round 0 120-145ms (from 179ms), STARK excl trace 1046-1071ms\n5. APC 100 for completeness\n6. If APC 300 passes but Round 0 savings < 25ms: profile batch path overhead with tracing spans to identify whether descriptor building, extraction, or eval dominates\n\n## Rollback Criteria\n\n- **Hard revert**: APC 0 STARK excl trace regresses >20ms vs 1784ms\n- **Hard revert**: Verification failure at any APC config\n- **Hard revert**: GPU OOM, `cudaErrorIllegalAddress`, or GPU hang at any APC config\n- **Soft revert**: APC 300 Round 0 improvement <10ms\n- **Soft revert**: APC 300 STARK excl trace improvement <20ms\n"}}
