{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Vbft5Qio9Vi55wyPnrinYa","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# 2026-04-15-1800-reenable-batch-round0-small-airs\n2\t\n3\tRe-enable the batch Round 0 descriptor-array kernel path for small AIRs, which was previously implemented (commits 0d1bb2f9, bcb1c0d2) but reverted due to GPU OOM at APC 100/300. The OOM blocker has since been resolved by the VPMM page size increase (16 MiB) and PRUNE_SHMEM_KERNELS, as confirmed by the current successful APC 300 benchmark run (1106ms STARK excl trace). At APC 300, ~250 small coset-parallel AIRs per segment currently require ~1000 individual kernel launches in Round 0; batching them into 2-4 descriptor-array kernel launches is expected to reduce Round 0 from 179ms to ~140-155ms, saving 25-40ms on STARK excl trace.\n4\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01R6kMM65U6pPfUMMgWraCe7","session_id":"f245fed0-0457-4d6a-9da2-744553774a6f","uuid":"a436710c-9235-4788-b42c-27547035aa84","timestamp":"2026-04-15T16:15:50.245Z"}
