{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Us9zqBnqcCSqZsQCcigsXW","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Plan: Re-enable Batch Round 0 Descriptor-Array Kernels for Small AIRs\n2\t\n3\t## Goal\n4\t\n5\tReduce Round 0 wall-clock time at APC 300 by batching the eval kernels for ~250 small coset-parallel AIRs per segment into 2-4 descriptor-array kernel launches on the default stream, then letting Phase 2 worker threads handle extraction for batched AIRs alongside full processing of the remaining ~60 large AIRs. This eliminates ~500 eval kernel launches per segment plus the per-AIR CPU overhead (`SymbolicConstraints::from`, DAG build, rule encode) for batched AIRs, without serializing extraction onto the critical path.\n6\t\n7\tCurrent: Round 0 = 179ms (90ms/seg). Expected after: Round 0 = 145-165ms (73-83ms/seg). Estimated net savings: 15-35ms on STARK excl trace (1106ms → 1071-1091ms).\n8\t\n9\tPrevious implementations (commits `0c699f47`, `bcb1c0d2`, `0d1bb2f9`) were reverted due to GPU OOM at APC 100/300. The OOM has since been resolved (VPMM 16 MiB page size + PRUNE_SHMEM_KERNELS), confirmed by the current APC 300 run at 1106ms.\n10\t\n11\t## Current Code Path\n12\t\n13\t**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n14\t\n15\t### Phase 1 (single-threaded, lines 1022-1198)\n16\tBuilds `Vec<Round0AirWorkItem>` for all AIRs with proving key refs, trace pointers, pre-computed buffer sizes, eq_3bs, and `Round0ExtractTables`. Items sorted by descending height. Percentile buffer sizes computed for per-thread pre-allocation.\n17\t\n18\t### Phase 1.5 (overlapped background, lines 1341-1382)\n19\tBackground thread uploads `d_eq_3b_per_trace` and precomputes `logup_combinations`, concurrent with Phase 2.\n20\t\n21\t### Phase 2 (multi-threaded, lines 1319-1413)\n22\t8 OS threads, per-thread CUDA streams, round-robin assignment. Per AIR: `process_air_round0()` at `round0.rs` does:\n23\t1. `evaluate_round0_zerocheck_gpu()` → zerocheck eval + reduction (~2 kernel launches)\n24\t2. `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu()` → CPU rule construction (`SymbolicConstraints::from`, DAG, encode, H2D) + logup eval + reduction (~2 kernel launches)\n25\t3. `_round0_extract_zerocheck_poly()` → GPU extraction to `d_batch_array` (1 kernel launch)\n26\t4. `_round0_extract_logup_polys()` → GPU extraction to `d_batch_array` (1 kernel launch)\n27\t\n28\tAt APC 300: ~312 AIRs/seg, ~6 kernel launches/AIR = ~1872 launches/seg. Wall clock: ~90ms/seg.\n29\t\n30\t### Why it's slow at APC 300\n31\tThe ~250 small AIRs (coset-parallel, height ≤ 256) each take ~0.2ms CPU work + ~0.1ms GPU eval + ~0.1ms extraction = ~0.4ms total. Across 8 threads: 31 per thread × 0.4ms ≈ 12ms. The remaining ~60 large AIRs take ~3-10ms each, ~8 per thread, total ~24-40ms. But measured per-segment Round 0 is ~90ms, with the difference attributable to CUDA driver overhead, stream scheduling, and memory pool contention across 1872 kernel launches.\n32\t\n33\t## Changes\n34\t\n35\t### Change 0: Diagnose the previous GPU hang\n36\t\n37\t**Before any code changes**, reproduce and diagnose the 12-minute GPU hang from commit `0d1bb2f9`:\n38\t1. Cherry-pick `0d1bb2f9` onto a throwaway branch\n39\t2. Build with debug symbols\n40\t3. Run: `compute-sanitizer --tool memcheck -- $PROVE_BIN prove --artifact apc300.cbor --input 0 --recursion`\n41\t4. If memcheck identifies an OOB access: note the location and fix in the new implementation\n42\t5. If no memcheck error: the hang was likely caused by the OOM (now resolved) — this de-risks the approach\n43\t6. Revert the cherry-pick\n44\t\n45\t### Change 1: Store logup Round 0 rules in proving key at keygen time\n46\t\n47\t**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/pkey.rs`\n48\t\n49\tAdd a `LogupRound0Rules` struct to `AirDataGpu` containing challenge-independent data only:\n50\t- `d_rules: DeviceBuffer<u128>` — encoded DAG rules on GPU\n51\t- `rules_len: usize` — number of rules\n52\t- `buffer_size: u32` — logup intermediates buffer size (already present as `logup_round0_buffer_size`)\n53\t- `dag_idx_to_rule_idx: Vec<usize>` — mapping from interaction index to rule index\n54\t\n55\t**NOT included** (challenge-dependent, computed per-proof):\n56\t- Interaction weight vectors (`numer_weights`, `denom_weights`, `denom_sum_init`) — these depend on `beta_pows` and `eq_3bs` and must be computed at proving time\n57\t\n58\tThese rules are used **ONLY by the batch path** (Change 4). Phase 2's `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu` is unchanged and continues to reconstruct rules per-AIR, preserving the GPU pacing.\n59\t\n60\t### Change 2: CUDA Batched Kernels\n61\t\n62\t**Files:**\n63\t- `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/zerocheck_round0.cu`\n64\t- `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/logup_round0.cu`\n65\t\n66\tReplicate the descriptor-array kernel design from reverted commit `0d1bb2f9`:\n67\t\n68\t- **`batched_zerocheck_r0_coset_parallel_kernel`**: Block-to-AIR mapping via `Round0BlockCtx` array. Each `Round0ZcCtx` descriptor has per-AIR parameters (main/preprocessed pointers, constraint config, eq_xis, sels, intermediates offset, output offset). Only `GLOBAL=true, NEEDS_SHMEM=false` instantiation. Uses the existing single-AIR kernel body with a descriptor lookup preamble.\n69\t\n70\t- **`batched_logup_r0_coset_parallel_kernel`**: Same pattern with `Round0LogupCtx` descriptors. Uses keygen-time rules from Change 1 (device pointers in descriptor) plus proving-time interaction weights (computed in Change 4).\n71\t\n72\t- **`batched_final_reduce_block_sums`**: Reuse the existing reduction pattern from `batch_mle.cu`.\n73\t\n74\t**Null intermediates safety:** Descriptors for AIRs with `buffer_size == 0` get the arena base pointer as their intermediates pointer. The kernel guards intermediates writes with `if (buffer_size > 0)`. The `cudaErrorIllegalAddress` from commit `0c699f47` was caused by unconditional intermediates dereference; this guard prevents it.\n75\t\n76\t### Change 3: FFI Bindings\n77\t\n78\t**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs`\n79\t\n80\tAdd `#[repr(C)]` Rust structs:\n81\t- `Round0BlockCtx { air_idx: u32, local_block_idx_x: u32 }`\n82\t- `Round0ZcCtx` — main_trace_ptr, preprocessed_ptr, buffer_size, num_x, skip_domain, num_cosets, eq_xis_ptr, sels_ptr, intermediates_offset, output_offset\n83\t- `Round0LogupCtx` — trace ptrs, d_rules_ptr, rules_len, d_numer_weights_ptr, d_denom_weights_ptr, buffer_size, d_eq_3b_ptr, intermediates_offset, output_offset\n84\t\n85\tAdd extern \"C\" declarations and safe Rust wrappers.\n86\t\n87\t### Change 4: Batch Orchestration Module\n88\t\n89\t**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0_batched.rs` (new file)\n90\t\n91\tAll public functions `#[inline(never)]`.\n92\t\n93\t**`identify_batchable_airs(work_items, l_skip) -> Vec<bool>`**\n94\t- Batchable if: (a) coset-parallel (`num_x * skip_domain < 32768`), (b) intermediates within budget (`< 16M Fp` per AIR), (c) AIR has zerocheck constraints or logup interactions\n95\t- Returns all-false if fewer than `MIN_BATCHABLE_AIRS = 50` qualify\n96\t- **Also** computes and logs the aggregate intermediates size for the reviewer's L2 cache concern: `info!(\"Batch Round 0: {} AIRs, aggregate intermediates: {} MB\", count, total_bytes / 1_000_000)`\n97\t\n98\t**`batch_round0_eval_only(work_items, batch_mask, pk, d_batch_ptr, ...) -> Result<BatchEvalState>`**\n99\tThis function runs on the default stream and performs **only the eval kernels**, NOT extraction. Returns a `BatchEvalState` containing per-AIR result pointers and metadata needed for extraction.\n100\t\n101\tSteps:\n102\t1. Group batchable AIRs by `num_cosets_zc` (constraint_degree − 1)\n103\t2. For each group:\n104\t   a. Compute total intermediates size (sum of per-AIR `zc_intermed_cap + logup_intermed_cap`)\n105\t   b. Allocate shared intermediates arena `DeviceBuffer`\n106\t   c. Build `Round0ZcCtx` descriptors with arena offsets\n107\t   d. Build `Round0BlockCtx` mapping\n108\t   e. Upload descriptors to GPU\n109\t   f. Launch `batched_zerocheck_r0_coset_parallel_kernel` + reduction\n110\t   g. Compute proving-time interaction weights per AIR (CPU: ~10μs/AIR using `beta_pows` and `eq_3bs`)\n111\t   h. Upload `d_numer_weights`, `d_denom_weights` to GPU\n112\t   i. Build `Round0LogupCtx` descriptors using keygen-time rules from `pk.per_air[air_idx].other_data.logup_round0_rules`\n113\t   j. Launch `batched_logup_r0_coset_parallel_kernel` + reduction\n114\t3. Return `BatchEvalState` with per-AIR eval result offsets into the intermediates arena\n115\t\n116\t**Key design: extraction is NOT done here.** Extraction is deferred to Phase 2 worker threads (Change 5).\n117\t\n118\t### Change 5: Integration\n119\t\n120\t**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n121\t\n122\tInsert the batch eval between Phase 1 (after `current_stream_sync()` at line 1202) and the `num_threads` branch:\n123\t\n124\t```rust\n125\t// Batch eval for small AIRs (default stream)\n126\tlet batch_mask = round0_batched::identify_batchable_airs(&work_items, l_skip);\n127\tlet batch_eval_state = if batch_mask.iter().any(|&b| b) {\n128\t    let state = round0_batched::batch_round0_eval_only(\n129\t        &work_items, &batch_mask, self.pk,\n130\t        d_batch_array.as_mut_ptr(), l_skip,\n131\t        &self.eq_3b_per_trace, &self.beta_pows,\n132\t    )?;\n133\t    current_stream_sync()?; // batch eval results visible to all streams\n134\t    Some(state)\n135\t} else {\n136\t    None\n137\t};\n138\t```\n139\t\n140\tIn Phase 2 worker threads, handle batched AIRs with extraction-only:\n141\t```rust\n142\tfor &item_idx in &thread_items[thread_id] {\n143\t    if batch_mask[item_idx] {\n144\t        // Batch eval already done; only run extraction\n145\t        let w = &work_items[item_idx];\n146\t        round0_batched::extract_batched_air(\n147\t            w, &batch_eval_state.as_ref().unwrap(),\n148\t            batch_ptr_val as *mut EF, &extract_tables,\n149\t        )?;\n150\t    } else {\n151\t        // Full per-AIR processing (eval + extraction, unchanged)\n152\t        process_air_round0(&work_items[item_idx], &mut bufs, batch_ptr_val as *mut EF, &extract_tables)?;\n153\t    }\n154\t}\n155\t```\n156\t\n157\t**Single-threaded path** (`num_threads <= 1`, lines 1280-1318): The batch path is skipped because `identify_batchable_airs` returns all-false (< 50 AIRs at APC 0). If somehow triggered, the single-threaded path would also check `batch_mask` — but this is a no-op since the mask is all-false.\n158\t\n159\t### Change 6: Visibility\n160\t\n161\tWiden `Round0AirWorkItem` and `Round0ExtractTables` to `pub(super)` and place `round0_batched.rs` as a submodule of `logup_zerocheck`.\n162\t\n163\t## Savings Breakdown (per segment at APC 300)\n164\t\n165\t| Component | Current | After | Change | Source |\n166\t|-----------|---------|-------|--------|--------|\n167\t| Batch eval (default stream) | 0ms | 5-8ms | +5-8ms | New: descriptor build + batched kernel |\n168\t| Small AIR CPU work in Phase 2 | ~6ms/thread | 0ms | −6ms | Eliminated: skip SymbolicConstraints::from, rule build |\n169\t| Small AIR eval launches in Phase 2 | ~5ms/thread | 0ms | −5ms | Eliminated: ~31 AIRs × 6 launches × 10μs |\n170\t| Small AIR extraction in Phase 2 | ~3ms/thread | ~3ms/thread | 0ms | Unchanged: extraction runs on worker threads |\n171\t| Large AIR processing in Phase 2 | ~40ms (max thread) | ~40ms (max thread) | 0ms | Unchanged |\n172\t| CUDA overhead (scheduling, pool) | ~36ms | ~20-30ms | −6-16ms | Fewer kernel launches = less driver overhead |\n173\t| **Total per segment** | **~90ms** | **~68-81ms** | **−9-22ms** | |\n174\t| **Total (2 segments)** | **179ms** | **135-162ms** | **17-44ms** | |\n175\t\n176\tThe improvement is driven by: (1) eliminating ~11ms/thread of small-AIR CPU+launch overhead, and (2) reducing systemic CUDA driver overhead from fewer total kernel launches (~1872 → ~1372 per segment, a 27% reduction).\n177\t\n178\t## Invariants\n179\t\n180\t1. **Correctness**: Batched eval produces the same coset-parallel NTT + constraint evaluation as per-AIR eval. Extraction uses the identical per-AIR kernels and writes to the same `d_batch_array` offsets.\n181\t\n182\t2. **APC 0 guard**: `MIN_BATCHABLE_AIRS = 50` disables batching (APC 0 has ~20 AIRs/seg).\n183\t\n184\t3. **Phase 2 pacing preserved**: Phase 2 is unchanged for non-batched (large) AIRs. Per-AIR `SymbolicConstraints::from()` + rule building remain as GPU pacing for large AIRs.\n185\t\n186\t4. **Stream ordering**: Batch eval on default stream → `current_stream_sync()` → Phase 2 on per-thread streams. Batch eval results are visible before any extraction runs.\n187\t\n188\t5. **Extraction concurrency preserved**: Extraction for batched AIRs runs on Phase 2 worker threads (not the default stream), maintaining 8-way concurrent extraction just like the current code.\n189\t\n190\t6. **L2 cache budget**: The aggregate intermediates arena for ~250 small AIRs is logged at runtime. Expected size: 10-50MB (well within 72MB L2). If > 72MB, the L2 thrashing documented in `batch-global-gkr-input-eval` would apply and we'd see a regression — caught by measurement.\n191\t\n192\t7. **Null pointer safety**: Descriptors with `buffer_size == 0` get arena base pointer + kernel guards writes with `if (buffer_size > 0)`.\n193\t\n194\t## Measurement Plan\n195\t\n196\t1. **Step 0**: Run `compute-sanitizer --tool memcheck` on cherry-picked `0d1bb2f9` at APC 300\n197\t2. Build: `cd /home/georg/powdr && cargo build --bin powdr_openvm_riscv -r --features \"metrics,cuda\"`\n198\t3. APC 0: verify Round 0 ≤ 180ms, STARK excl trace ≤ 1810ms\n199\t4. APC 300: expect Round 0 135-162ms (from 179ms), STARK excl trace 1062-1089ms\n200\t5. APC 100 for completeness\n201\t6. If Round 0 savings < 10ms: add tracing spans inside `batch_round0_eval_only` to identify bottleneck (descriptor build vs eval vs weight computation)\n202\t\n203\t## Rollback Criteria\n204\t\n205\t- **Hard revert**: APC 0 STARK excl trace regresses >20ms vs 1784ms\n206\t- **Hard revert**: Verification failure at any APC config\n207\t- **Hard revert**: GPU OOM, `cudaErrorIllegalAddress`, or GPU hang at any APC config\n208\t- **Soft revert**: APC 300 Round 0 improvement <10ms\n209\t- **Soft revert**: APC 300 STARK excl trace improvement <15ms\n210\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01RS5ZqxNfusht1ytueLXki3","session_id":"f245fed0-0457-4d6a-9da2-744553774a6f","uuid":"a1930b82-7cb3-4a4b-afaa-7f4954a61754","timestamp":"2026-04-15T17:01:15.186Z"}
